{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless","id":1483924,"title":"Is Oblivion worthless?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-13T15:34:02-07:00","id":1483924,"title":"Is Oblivion worthless?","content":"Am I right in thinking that 20% risk of 1 stain isn't a tradeoff worth doing for any Oblivion power?<br /> <br /> <br /> Some quick math. Most starting characters have Humanity 6, and no rouse check re-roll. This means, that one single stain gives them 25% risk of losing Humanity at the end of the session. If they have Humanity 7, the risk increases to 33%, Losing Humanity is very bad, as there's no clear rules for regaining it (some GMs might not even allow it), and the only way to do it by the rules as written costs so much exp that you will never ever afford it in any reasonable campaign. Low Humanity has crippling maluses to social rolls, and is also not necessarily something you want to portray even if you want to play a Lasombra or a necromancer.<br /> <br /> personally, this is seriously putting me off playing Lasombra or Cappadocians/Giovanni, two of my favorite clans, and whenever I am GM, I will always do away with the stains-for-Oblivion rule. I'm considering trying to get the GM for an upcoming V5 dark ages campaign I'm gonna be a player in to do the same.<br /> <br /> It feels to me like the designers who wrote Oblivion haven't even played their own game, and doesn't realize how harsh 1 stain is. I've seen player characters lose Humanity because of one single stain several times.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 06-13-2022, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T17:14:48-07:00","id":1483934,"title":"","content":"It's kind of the D&amp;D equivalent of permanently losing a point in one of your stats for casting a spell. Is it really worth what you're going to lose? No. Add to that the fact that you have to spend xp to take the risk? Hard no. <br /> <br /> There's a reason D&amp;D moved away from this model in 3rd Edition, before which things like Resurrection or Haste aged you by a year. It's a bad mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","user":"Hades","date":". 06-13-2022, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T17:33:03-07:00","id":1483936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> here's a reason D&amp;D moved away from this model in 3rd Edition, before which things like Resurrection or Haste aged you by a year. It's a bad mechanic. </div> </div> </div>By the way, this reminds me of <i>The Bloodsoaked Saint\u2019s Resurrection</i>. Why on Earth does it state that it costs a <i>permanent</i> road dot. Actually, it's even worse and it's a freaking level 9 power combination","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-13-2022, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T18:01:54-07:00","id":1483937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483936#post1483936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, this reminds me of <i>The Bloodsoaked Saint\u2019s Resurrection</i>. Why on Earth does it state that it costs a <i>permanent</i> road dot. Actually, it's even worse and it's a freaking level 9 power combination</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...What? What book is that from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T18:33:55-07:00","id":1483942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless#post1483924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels to me like the designers who wrote Oblivion haven't even played their own game, and doesn't realize how harsh 1 stain is. I've seen player characters lose Humanity because of one single stain several times.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as the writers having picked out the clans they want you to play, and the Lasombra and Hecata aren't on the list. They're excluded from the core rulebook for a reason. They're NPC's. <br /> <br /> I don't agree with it, in fact I loathe it, but this is how I'm reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 06-13-2022, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T18:54:06-07:00","id":1483943,"title":"","content":"V5 rules are not so great and tying Disciplines to permanent loss of character stats, especially when it's something like, &quot;Any time you use your clan's signature discipline, you have a 1 in 5 chance to permanently lose stats on your character at the end of the session&quot; is just terribad. Ignore it. Throw that rule into the trash. Take it out behind the metaphorical shed and shoot it in its big dumb stupid face. Don't feel bad about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-13-2022, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T19:28:54-07:00","id":1483946,"title":"","content":"It only costs Humanity, not Path Rating, so realistically all older Lasombra and Hecata should be on Paths, most likely Death and the Soul in the latter case. I don't think it's a problem that they made Oblivion cost Humanity, so much as that they have no PC method of adopting a Path of Enlightenment available. They basically made Oblivion a Path only power, then banished players from being on Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-13-2022, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T20:30:20-07:00","id":1483951,"title":"","content":"I see what they were doing, but it is stupid. In past editions, Necromancy and Obtenebration were pretty messed up, to a point a character on Humanity <b><i>should</i></b> make a degeneration check when using them recklessly.<br /> <br /> Now here's the thing, I am a rules lawyer. So, my first reaction was to see if there was anything that could mitigate this RAW. Turns out, no. Convictions can mitigate stains gained by violating Tenets, but nothing else. A good ST would, and should, allow Convictions to mitigate all stains when you gain them in service of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T21:37:04-07:00","id":1483954,"title":"","content":"If you want to make Oblivion more functional, but you kinda like the whole idea that it's uniquely prone to degrading Humanity, a simple house rule to replace the random Stain on Rouse checks thing:<br /> <br /> Anytime your actions would cause you to gain a Stain while using or benefiting from Oblivion, increase the number of Stains incurred by 1.<br /> <br /> This leaves things largely in the players' hands as they'd have to choose to use Oblivion to do things that generate Stains in the first place, and makes how bad Oblivion is more contextual to the game being run. Chronicle Tenets of the &quot;be a good person,&quot; type are going to be harsh... but the Hecata and Lasombra aren't that well suited to such styles in the first place. A Chronicle Tenet set that wouldn't be punishing towards vigilantism and other justification for violence and fright would give you some decent space to find a niche for an Oblivion user that's not a one way ticket to wight-dom. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T21:38:31-07:00","id":1483955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483951#post1483951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what they were doing, but it is stupid. In past editions, Necromancy and Obtenebration were pretty messed up, to a point a character on Humanity <b><i>should</i></b> make a degeneration check when using them recklessly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, they're just disciplines and not much different from any other, just that they're creepier. I don't think players should have to make Degeneration checks for using those anymore than they should have to make checks for using Thaumaturgy or Chimerstry. I don't even think even Daimoinian or Dark Thaumaturgy required checks to see if you lose Humanity for using them. Should always come down to what you <i>do</i> with a Discipline that determines whether you make checks to lose Humanity (or gain Stains in 5th edition). Losing Humanity because you decided to make a room a little darker or peeked across the Shroud to see if there's a ghost around is not a good rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T22:52:32-07:00","id":1483959,"title":"","content":"I have played as a Lasombra during two years a weekly chronicle and never received a stain, my character had Oblivion 3. It really depends on how much you rely on the disciplines, how much you roll dices in your storytelling style and the discipline powers. The level 1 powers do not produce stains, as they do not roll hunger, in consequence, only Arms of Ahriman (of my powers) had the risk.<br /> <br /> I found Oblivion very rewarding and thematic, you feel the risk as the corruption of the abyss lurking you, you have to dossificate the use of the discipline. And, in particular, even being not particularly powerful in terms of damage, I realized that Arms of Ahriman is a very good power, the only combat power from distance (at least at reach of a neonate).<br /> <br /> The other two powers I had were Oblivion sight and Shadow play, being able to see spirits and still navigate the darkness and being able to use shadows to intimidate and stealth.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed Oblivion as a Lasombra, although I suspect that playing an Hecata or an abyss mystic, with all the ceremonies, it would be trickier. But to me, the risk of stains never was a problem and, mathematically, is very low with characters of Humanity 5-6, that would be the &quot;usual&quot; Oblivion practitioner.<br /> <br /> For example, a character with Humanity 6, after failing the 20% probability to have an stain, should also fail another 25 % probability to degenerate. The accumulated probability of losing humanity is 5%, when using a power. That means that you only lose humanity around 1 of 20 times using Oblivion &quot;hunger&quot; levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 06-14-2022, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T22:59:50-07:00","id":1483961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483942#post1483942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read it as the writers having picked out the clans they want you to play, and the Lasombra and Hecata aren't on the list. They're excluded from the core rulebook for a reason. They're NPC's.<br /> <br /> I don't agree with it, in fact I loathe it, but this is how I'm reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hecata are the single most supported clan in the entire 5th edition. They have more loresheets than most other clans combined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T00:12:30-07:00","id":1483968,"title":"","content":"Absolutely, Lasombra and Hecata are protagonists of 5th edition, the former having an entire chronicle and a by night with them as the main focus, the others having almost a clanbook and ten bloodlines, with a wide arrange of powers and disciplines. This two are more important in lore and systems than Banu Haqim or Ministry, attending to the books content. If there are &quot;forgotten&quot; clans in 5th, this are the Companion ones. But the Lasombra and Hecata are the best and deepest well developed of the 15 clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T04:07:26-07:00","id":1483975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483955#post1483955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't even think even Daimoinian or Dark Thaumaturgy required checks to see if you lose Humanity for using them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I unfortunately can. There's an optional rule in V20 to make Daimoinon and Dark Thaum cause a degeneration check whenever they're used by someone on humanity <i>Or Any Path</i> that isn't road of sin.<br /> <br /> Like most people I know, I ignore it and anyone who tries to enforce it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T04:08:29-07:00","id":1483976,"title":"","content":"If you prefer, you can just pinch the V20DA approach to Necromancy, where there are sequelae for using those powers (V20DA Time of Secrets, p.53). You could adapt something similar for the Abyss Mysticism/Obtenebration powers, making them more Abyssal in nature. Some of the Abyssal monsters in that book would make really cool enemies to encounter if something goes horribly wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T05:07:27-07:00","id":1483981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483937#post1483937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...What? What book is that from?</div> </div> </div> </div>DAV20. There was a tier of backers that allowed submission of a bespoke combo-discipline. It seems very likely that was one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T05:54:23-07:00","id":1483982,"title":"","content":"Pretty much yeah, I removed that mechanic and re-seperated necromancy and Obtenebretion to balance out the buff. Its a silly discipline anyway as written in v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T05:58:34-07:00","id":1483983,"title":"","content":"Don't want to rain on the parade too much but as bad as Oblivion is, in V5, the general rule is that you're really better off investing in mundane skills and backgrounds rather than disciplines. There's a few gems you can try to nab at character creation but the abilities that are &quot;good&quot; mostly appear too late and require unreal investment for the short timeframe of most chronicles. Many abilities are extremely situational or can be done better with mundane tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:06:55-07:00","id":1483988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483955#post1483955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehh, they're just disciplines and not much different from any other, just that they're creepier. I don't think players should have to make Degeneration checks for using those anymore than they should have to make checks for using Thaumaturgy or Chimerstry. I don't even think even Daimoinian or Dark Thaumaturgy required checks to see if you lose Humanity for using them. Should always come down to what you <i>do</i> with a Discipline that determines whether you make checks to lose Humanity (or gain Stains in 5th edition). Losing Humanity because you decided to make a room a little darker or peeked across the Shroud to see if there's a ghost around is not a good rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obtenebration powers tend to invoke primal fear in those who witness it and cause extremely slow and painful death in the form of suffocation. Necromancy is actually worse most of the time. Necromancy often does things like cause inherent suffering, enslaving of others, and death. Of all the main disciplines, these are the easiest to use recklessly, and even to the point of causing death and suffering. In fact, it is so easy, most users of these disciplines take on paths of enlightenment to avoid the hard moral questions.<br /> <br /> Now yes, I do still agree with you that it should depend on how they're used. However, these disciplines specifically are the most likely to be used in morally questionable ways.<br /> <br /> <s>Also, Daimonian and Dark Thaumaturgy require degeneration as per an optional rule, but that's optional.</s>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:18:38-07:00","id":1483990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483988#post1483988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obtenebration powers tend to invoke primal fear in those who witness it and cause extremely slow and painful death in the form of suffocation. Necromancy is actually worse most of the time. Necromancy often does things like cause inherent suffering, enslaving of others, and death. Of all the main disciplines, these are the easiest to use recklessly, and even to the point of causing death and suffering. In fact, it is so easy, most users of these disciplines take on paths of enlightenment to avoid the hard moral questions.<br /> <br /> Now yes, I do still agree with you that it should depend on how they're used. However, these disciplines specifically are the most likely to be used in morally questionable ways.<br /> <br /> <s>Also, Daimonian and Dark Thaumaturgy require degeneration as per an optional rule, but that's optional.</s></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that then mean the action of causing suffering or killing would provoke a stain? As opposed to the power itself? What's the difference between defending yourself from a violent person and choking him out vs defending yourself from a violent person with some Obtenebration in the lungs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:46:25-07:00","id":1483997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483990#post1483990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't that then mean the action of causing suffering or killing would provoke a stain? As opposed to the power itself? What's the difference between defending yourself from a violent person and choking him out vs defending yourself from a violent person with some Obtenebration in the lungs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It very much would IMO! Like I said in a pervious post, &quot;<i><b>I see what they were doing, but it is stupid.</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the weapon verse the wielder argument. Is the weapon itself inherently evil? No. The weapon could be used in defense of others. The main reason Oblivion likely gives a stain is the popular depiction of Necromancy.<br /> <br /> \u200bNecromancy is almost always seen as evil in popular media. This comes from years of several different cultures and beliefs dictating it as such. In <s>Jewish and</s> Christan belief, Necromancy is seen as a sorcery that involves you communing with demons. So, many writers of Necromancy in various games, movies, and stories in general tend to have some kind of corrupting element to it. In the case of V5, you're tapping into the very concept of Oblivion itself. A concept so inherently soul crushing that it eats away at one's sanity just by using it. After all, what does humanity fear more then the <b><i>unknown and death</i></b>?<br /> <br /> Still with Humanity costing as much as it does in V5, the risk is not worth the reward. The powers are on par with other discipline powers, which is the problem! Why risk your character, when it's no better than blood sorcery! Hell blood sorcery in V5 is objectively better than Oblivion at everything!!!!<br /> <br /> Sorry personal rant aside, I agree Oblivion is not a well-designed ability. I do like it, but I could spend all day poking holes at my favorite V5 discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 06-14-2022, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:55:06-07:00","id":1483999,"title":"","content":"Personal rants are Best rants. I agree with everything you said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26764_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26764\" data-vbnamecard=\"26764\">Vilenecromancer</a> . Im sure we could have quite the discussion on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T10:57:28-07:00","id":1484006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483997#post1483997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Jewish and Christan belief, Necromancy is seen as a sorcery that involves you communing with demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... no?<br /> <br /> The Torah explicitly forbids using magic to communicate with the dead, and the most clear line about this also says Jews are forbidden from &quot;sorcery&quot; in terms of dealing with non-human spirits. Judaism literally says dealing with &quot;demons&quot; and speaking to the dead are two different forms of off-limits magic for Jews to practice. Please don't shove Medieval Christian theologians making stuff up on Jews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:03:22-07:00","id":1484020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484006#post1484006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... no?<br /> <br /> The Torah explicitly forbids using magic to communicate with the dead, and the most clear line about this also says Jews are forbidden from &quot;sorcery&quot; in terms of dealing with non-human spirits. Judaism literally says dealing with &quot;demons&quot; and speaking to the dead are two different forms of off-limits magic for Jews to practice. Please don't shove Medieval Christian theologians making stuff up on Jews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","user":"Hades","date":". 06-14-2022, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:04:19-07:00","id":1484021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484006#post1484006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... no?<br /> <br /> The Torah explicitly forbids using magic to communicate with the dead, and the most clear line about this also says Jews are forbidden from &amp;quot;sorcery&amp;quot; in terms of dealing with non-human spirits. Judaism literally says dealing with &amp;quot;demons&amp;quot; and speaking to the dead are two different forms of off-limits magic for Jews to practice. Please don't shove Medieval Christian theologians making stuff up on Jews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. I'm sorry for not being specific and being culturally insensitive. My point is still the same, Necromancy being seen as wrong in some way, BUT you are right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:28:34-07:00","id":1484041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484020#post1484020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh boy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand my phrasing is a bit strong but... it's pretty well documented thanks to the Vatican liking to keep records.<br /> <br /> To vastly oversimplify things: the Roman Catholic church decreed that actual necromancy wasn't real, and was a trick by Satan that fooled people into thinking they were speaking to the dead when they were actually speaking to demons, in order to reconcile a mistranslation that occurred when the Bible was translated through multiple languages (and the cultural influences of those languages with vastly different conceptualizations of evil spirits and the afterlife) and the belief that the translations approved by the Church were divinely inspired (aka shouldn't be called into question as possibly mistranslated). So when &quot;you shouldn't practice sorcery, and you shouldn't practice necromancy,&quot; morphed in, &quot;you shouldn't practice sorcery, which is necromancy,&quot; they had to invent a theological explanation of how talking to the dead was the same as consorting with evil spirits.<br /> <br /> Which is then the basis for all of the &quot;evil necromancer&quot; tropes Vilenecromaner is talking about (and lots of other things like the panic over Ouija boards during the spiritualist revival because of fears that it would get people possessed by demons while they were trying to contact dead people).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484021#post1484021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is still the same, Necromancy being seen as wrong in some way</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, and I didn't mean to call into question the general point of how necromancy changed in mainstream perception over time to what it means to people now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T04:49:54-07:00","id":1484102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484041#post1484041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand my phrasing is a bit strong but... it's pretty well documented thanks to the Vatican liking to keep records.<br /> <br /> To vastly oversimplify things: the Roman Catholic church decreed that actual necromancy wasn't real, and was a trick by Satan that fooled people into thinking they were speaking to the dead when they were actually speaking to demons, in order to reconcile a mistranslation that occurred when the Bible was translated through multiple languages (and the cultural influences of those languages with vastly different conceptualizations of evil spirits and the afterlife) and the belief that the translations approved by the Church were divinely inspired (aka shouldn't be called into question as possibly mistranslated). So when &amp;quot;you shouldn't practice sorcery, and you shouldn't practice necromancy,&amp;quot; morphed in, &amp;quot;you shouldn't practice sorcery, which is necromancy,&amp;quot; they had to invent a theological explanation of how talking to the dead was the same as consorting with evil spirits.<br /> <br /> Which is then the basis for all of the &amp;quot;evil necromancer&amp;quot; tropes Vilenecromaner is talking about (and lots of other things like the panic over Ouija boards during the spiritualist revival because of fears that it would get people possessed by demons while they were trying to contact dead people).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm not disagreeing with you. Pretty much every Pagan European culture had a pretty good understanding of differentiating non human spirits from dead humans become shades, and if when you die you either go to Heaven, Purgatory or Hell you by definition must adopt the position the Catholic church took. Medieval magical texts are rife with these kinds of ludicrous ideas brought over from the Church (and not just about necromancy). <br /> <br /> An interesting side point, the people I know who actually practice necromancy in real life as an actual spiritual practice and not some new age BS are all quite the socially aggressive and domineering types (and they all seem to have careers in money, for whatever reason). I can understand how they'd get a bad rap and be considered evil, though I wouldn't personally call them so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T15:09:59-07:00","id":1484140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483946#post1483946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only costs Humanity, not Path Rating, so realistically all older Lasombra and Hecata should be on Paths, most likely Death and the Soul in the latter case. I don't think it's a problem that they made Oblivion cost Humanity, so much as that they have no PC method of adopting a Path of Enlightenment available. They basically made Oblivion a Path only power, then banished players from being on Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is stretching things as far as analyzing their intentions goes, precisely because they originally had no intention to even mention Paths ever again (lets face it, even the shitty depiction of Paths rules-wise in the Sabbat book was a compromise, not a plan). As far as the actual, official V5 rules go, your take doesn't exist and can't exist.<br /> <br /> On the merit of doing it... I disagree that this is fine. It could be for many pre-V5 power lines, including Abyss Mysticism, but Oblivion isn't Abyss Mysticism. It is regular Obtenebration + Necromancy (any Path). It doesn't make any sense to be bound to Humanity loss when no other Discipline is (Necromancy? Dominate and Presence should be tied to Humanity loss more than it. Obtenebration is the power Peter Pan less uses as a jerk).<br /> <br /> More than that, the game is still meant to support most groups using Humanity, and Oblivion is the Signature Discipline of a Main Clan. Making it prohibitive for regular play at a regular table is obnoxious design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483988#post1483988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now yes, I do still agree with you that it should depend on how they're used. However, these disciplines specifically are the most likely to be used in morally questionable ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem, outside how shitty the rule is from a design perspective as you perfectly elaborated upon, and that they don't need to be used like that just because they're good to use like that... is that even this tendency has a lot of caveats in the game.<br /> <br /> While the Giovanni Necromancy is a lot like that, most other bloodlines that used it had far less &quot;domineering&quot; approaches. Cappadocians and Samedi focused on blurring the lines between corpses and living bodies, Lamia is &quot;Alchemy of Depression&quot;, Nagaraja just pierces the Shroud or let the vampire do to ghosts what vampires do to everybody else. So the game actually has plenty of &quot;that's not actually any more evil than any common Discipline or actually even less&quot; Necromancy.<br /> <br /> Obtenebration induces less fear than Presence 2 and is far less lethal than almost anything else in a game that has Path of Blood, Quietus, Dominate, Dementation, Animalism and Presence. All those Disciplines have at least one power that can be easily far more cruel by itself than anything Obtenebration can pull off. It is just that &quot;Darkness Manipulation&quot; seems more showy and they liked to play a lot the idea of those powers being drawn from the Abyss, not because the powers themselves were evil.<br /> <br /> It was a play on the idea of the Lasombra being corrupted Catholics, and was better worked through Abyss Mysticism, that <b>isn't</b> regular Obtenebration. Both because it better represents dealings with the Abyss and because that leaves the main Discipline free for characters that won't explore this concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T20:36:22-07:00","id":1484172,"title":"","content":"If I were a Hecata I would get Shadow Play, Oblivion Sight, Resilience, Unswayable Mind, Fortress of the Inner Facade, Heightened Senses, and Sense the Unseen. \u2014 None of the other inclan disciplines are worth it. Out of clan you could get: Sense the Beast, Cloud Memory, Compel, etc.<br /> <br /> But as another said V5 is best played ignoring disciplines and focusing on Skills and backgrounds. Hunger Checks are not worth it even without Stains.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18512-uriel","name":"uriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T06:50:29-07:00","id":1484206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483976#post1483976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you prefer, you can just pinch the V20DA approach to Necromancy, where there are sequelae for using those powers (V20DA Time of Secrets, p.53). You could adapt something similar for the Abyss Mysticism/Obtenebration powers, making them more Abyssal in nature. Some of the Abyssal monsters in that book would make really cool enemies to encounter if something goes horribly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, rereading Players Guide to High Clans for DAV, there are already side effects listed for all the Abyssal Mysticism powers there. So there's already an alternative system that can be used instead of insta-stains.<br /> <br /> I know the powers aren't identical, but you can use the DAV and V20DA side effects/sequelae as good consequences for Oblivion powers that go wrong (if you want that sort of thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T07:51:53-07:00","id":1484211,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that the chance for losing Humanity when you use an Oblivion power is not all that high. It's a 1 in 5 chance for getting a stain, sure, but you get to make a remorse roll at the end of every session. The lower the character's humanity, the more likely they're going to pass the remorse roll. So yeah, an oblivion user is probably not going to stay at Humanity 7, but once they drop down to Humanity 5 or so, the chance of losing more gets pretty small. &quot;Accessing the Abyss inevitably erodes your soul&quot; is a design choice you can agree with or not, but it's not like the mechanics of it guarantee that your character will be shredded into a Wight in short order. If you see Humanity solely as a character sheet resource then I can see why this would bother you, but if you see it as a framework for storytelling, then it's more about how using Oblivion changes your character and less about how it makes your character lose stats. You didn't pay points for Humanity in character generation, you just got handed 7 or 8. Oblivion users will have less over time. Shrug. If you think the rate of Humanity loss is too fast, it's really easy to just say you only get a stain on a Rouse check result of 1, and if Humanity erosion from contact with the Abyss is not a theme you want to explore you can just ignore the stain cost like others have suggested. The game police aren't going to arrest you. But I don't think it's crazy to say that Oblivion is different from other disciplines and has a cost--it's a discipline that clearly interacts with forces outside of the user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T08:39:02-07:00","id":1484217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484211#post1484211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that the chance for losing Humanity when you use an Oblivion power is not all that high.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is still a burden with too many consequences for the character. It works well for a limited range of concepts, but not for everyone.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting, it won't be the only source of Stains, just the only one that doesn't depend on Chronicle Tenets and yet is guaranteed to come by regularly, as it is linked to a trait you paid for.<br /> <br /> Every time you take a Stain, the decision to use this power in the same session becomes harder. Using this power to do something that is worth a Stain by itself increases your risk significantly. If you use it frequently you're virtually guaranteed to take Stains regularly, and in a particularly unlucky session you may end up with two, three Stains at the end just from your own character sheet and dice rolls, or you stop to use the power altogether in the first Stain. The power, again, that you bought and is a clan staple.<br /> <br /> Those risks don't ever go away completely. Either you're conservative with your birthright when everyone else can use theirs all the time, or you're almost guaranteed to end every single session with a Stain. Or, from an in-character perspective, sense the effects of the Beast every damn week at least. It doesn't matter at this point that it becomes harder to fall as Humanity gets lower, you're playing against yourself all the time.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you get dangerously low, or just lower than your character concept, then no fancy description will change that Humanity costs XP. It doesn't &quot;just&quot; requires a shit-ton of in-game effort, without house-rules it also costs a <b>lot</b> of XP, stunting your character growth significantly. For, and I repeat, a clan staple.<br /> <br /> You'll just end up, one way or the other, with a character that can't use their signature power frequently and that actually behaves better than their Humanity rating indicates, since they need to compensate the extra Stains, which are exactly the opposite behavior you want to further in Hecata or Lasombra PCs if you want to follow the themes if the clans. It isn't impossible to think a character that fits the bill, but it is objectively bad game design for what it is meant to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T08:55:58-07:00","id":1484218,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it's fair to create a dichotomy between Humanity as a mechanical element and a story element. It's both. There are some pretty significant mechanics attached to Humanity. Dropping from Humanity 8 to Humanity 4 (esp. considering the XP values involved) is a drastic mechanical change in your character's ability to interact with humans, and remain hidden among them to those that know what to look for as penalties on social rolls increase and what Blush of Life can accomplish decreases.<br /> <br /> As well, the talk of odds tends to assume that the only Stains you're risking are Oblivion based ones (and at that, seem to be assuming you don't use Oblivion powers above level 1 more than once a session). If the session's activities have left the whole coterie with two Stains, but the Oblivion user didn't have luck on their side and got two extra ones (or that was statistically average because they rolled for a rouse ~10 times over the course of the session to activate Oblivion powers), that's a much faster track to low Humanity. <br /> <br /> Something that's sort of an on-going sticking point in V5 mechanics discussions is that some of new mechanics introduced in V5 are not easily adapted to different play styles; esp. regarding how much a group likes to toss dice. The game doesn't have any built-in dials to help adjust for the fact that some play groups are going to find the risk of Oblivion Stains incredibly minor (don't roll a lot in general, use of Disciplines as a last resort, low ratio of scenes to sessions), while others can easily feel it way harder.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T09:01:47-07:00","id":1484219,"title":"","content":"Using Convictions to counter the stains is a fun solution, and quite popular amongst the games I've played. <br /> <br /> When I was playing a Lasombra, I did use other disciplines besides Oblivion (by the end I had Oblivion 3, Potence 3 and Dominate 3). Potence was the one I used most frequently, be it for combat or utility, then Dominate tied with Oblivion. I only used Arms when it was the best option, for ambushes, reaching far away things or attacking something I don't want to get close. <br /> <br /> At the end, it is channeling power from where the dead go to die, Oblivion itself, having it be a costly preventing trivial uses isn't a bad thing imo. At the end, the Lasombra and Hecata have other equally valuable disciplines. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T09:26:52-07:00","id":1484221,"title":"","content":"As far as the thematic side of things...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why to keep debating it, but it's a real stretch to say that channeling the power of the spiritual curse that made you into a vampire to have superhuman strength enough to rip a human in half (Potence) doesn't carry extra risk towards Stains, but using the &quot;energy of Oblivion&quot; to create shadow tentacles to do it instead does. The complaint a lot of people have is that it's completely incoherent with what Humanity and Stains are meant to represent (losing touch with your former human self on the slow slide to pure monster as you fail to reconcile the actions you take over time). Vampires are undead parasites leeching off humanity. All of their powers are &quot;tainted&quot; but the &quot;energy&quot; of the dead because... they're dead things unnaturally running around stealing energy from the living to keep themselves going.<br /> <br /> It's also a new conceit to V5 that wasn't present in the previous editions. The lore was changed just to justify the extra cost to using Oblivion... which doesn't really demonstrate a strong reason to have an extra cost attached to it in practice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T09:38:34-07:00","id":1484222,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Others have stated it far better than I could. My main problem with it is that it is redundant (or rather, doubly punitive) because, as others have pointed out, using Oblivion to do wicked deeds is already going to get you Stains. So it's simply not needed, except as an artificial deterrent. And that deterrent impacts some playstyles more than others without any dials.<br /> <br /> But it's easy enough to ignore, for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T11:19:41-07:00","id":1484226,"title":"","content":"There's an implication behind all this: the implication that your humanity is actually your soul, and not just a representation of your psychological resistance to berzerker hunger and rage. The force behind Oblivion literally eats your soul bit at a time. The idea of a soul eating discipline is...familiar...to those of us who played earlier editions, and I didn't like it the last time.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm comfortable with the idea that someone with Humanity 8 literally has a bigger soul than someone with Humanity 7. I've always treated that number as representing something psychological, a unique form of insanity that gradually overcomes vampires because their human brains are not designed to deal with berzerker urges. But things like this strongly imply that, nah, it's not a form of insanity: your soul literally shrinks over time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T11:34:22-07:00","id":1484227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484219#post1484219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end, it is channeling power from where the dead go to die, Oblivion itself, having it be a costly preventing trivial uses isn't a bad thing imo. At the end, the Lasombra and Hecata have other equally valuable disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, this is not a reason, this is a justification. The rules exist to enforce a theme, the lore to justify the rules. The lore doesn't impact if the rules are good or not.<br /> <br /> Every clan has three Disciplines, one of them being a Signature of sorts. You don't need to follow the stereotype, but being able to is the whole point of the option. The concept of the Hecata is a Necromancer, the concept of the Lasombra is a Shadow Manipulator (the freaking clan's name is literally &quot;Theshadow&quot;). If the rule isn't conducive of making such characters, something is wrong. If the rule isn't giving the clan three usable Disciplines, the clan is crippled.<br /> <br /> If the power and/or the clan has a specific theme attached to it, the role of the rule, from a design standpoint, must be to encourage <i>the player</i> to follow the theme, even if its fluff punishes <i>the character</i>. Again, you want Hecata to be Necromancers and Lasombra to play with shadows. You also want them to be particularly prone to both act more deviously and seem less Humane.<br /> <br /> But by causing Stains, instead of making the player want to follow the theme, it tries to make the power force the theme. It backfires, as some players may want the extra challenge, but most will instead <b><i>avoid</i></b> <b><i>the very themes</i></b> the rule should be helping to foster. You said it yourself, instead of relying on it more you avoided your very signature power. It worked as <i>a</i> character fine, but by being contrary to the typical Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Nothing against your game or your character at all, but by making you act against the actual theme just for the character to work fine, the rule failed. It is plain bad game design.<br /> <br /> You want an example of how to make the rule actually foster the theme? Instead of causing Stains, Oblivion could be capped as the opposite of your Humanity (Humanity + Oblivion can't be more than 10) and in exchange it acts as a Conviction by itself once per session: your first act that would cause Stains causes 1 less Stain if done using Oblivion. Now you <b>want </b>to lower your Humanity when increasing the Discipline and get to act more depraved by using it.<br /> <br /> Second, for the theme, it has a history in the setting. And a part of the problem is that it is also ridiculous from the perspective of this history.<br /> <br /> Originally it was two very distinct Disciplines, Necromancy and Obtenebration. Necromancy has a theme of not being healthy in the very long term, but in the short therm it is just Death-themed magic and those long term effects are avoidable with common sense. More importantly, in all its forms it has a theme in VtM of bringing the vampire closer to the other side of their nature in a philosophical way. So it may be either damning or healthy for a vampire. It is also not overtly dangerous because the Dark Umbra isn't overtly dangerous.<br /> <br /> The other one, Obtenebration, had from the beginning a <i><u>legend</u></i> to it that it wasn't actual darkness, but a strange matters siphoned from another place, an alien dimension. Initially it was just for the Lovecraftian factor because they liked to &quot;sneak&quot; Lovecraftian themes in the Sabbat (at the time they really wanted to make the Sabbat be about the three-sides war between the Great Old Ones, Satanists and the Illuminati, on Earth and Beyond). But it had no side effects attached to it precisely because if it had it would be a certainty, not a legend, and most Lasombra would stop using it.<br /> <br /> When they decided to explore this theme further, they created the Abyss Mysticism, a Pseudo-Discipline with several powers that was more strongly thematic, and arguably stronger indeed, but that was attached to side effects from the contact with the Abyss. Being less Humane was common among Abyss Mysticism, but less because it required such and more because you had to be more than a little nuts to deal with that shit and its possible consequences, you still could be perfectly good and fine, though. The effects weren't moral, but strange mutations to body and mind, because it was less about dehumanizing thoughts and more about Lovecraftian transformation.<br /> <br /> V5 basically looked at this history, the role of the Abyss Mystics among the Lasombra, the many wise practitioners of Necromancy that weren't interested in enslaving ghosts, the body of secret vampiric knowledge on the Dark Umbra, the many characters, bloodlines and themes explored that way through the years, including a few heroic characters that wielded such powers... threw everything away and simplified the themes in the most direct and unrefined way possible.<br /> <br /> Do not take any of this as hateful, bitter criticism, though. I'm just explaining my position in more detail. V5 is turning both system and setting upside down. For all the direr criticism I have on other aspects of the new lore, here it is just a normal mistake when you're trying on new paths. The themes are complex and hard to nail at once, they were originally build over several books, through many, many years. The whole system is new, it needs tempering all over the place. I don't think this is a terrible mistake they can't be excused for. But it is, no way around it, a bad rule. Happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T15:21:50-07:00","id":1484239,"title":"","content":"Its probably worth noting oblivion theoretically covers mortis of the clan cappadocian whose discipline powers where comparatively neutral if grim compared to their giovanni successors and historically cappadocians where one of the less awful clans, then again I don't think it's possible to simulate mortis with Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-16-2022, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T16:04:56-07:00","id":1484241,"title":"","content":"The decision to combine Necromancy and Obteneration still seems so bizarre to me. Like someone decided that the Abyss and Oblivion should be the same thing. And then since Oblivion was in the Underworld, and since some of Necromancy's powers affect the Underworld or its inhabitants, then Necromancy and Obteneration must be the same thing... somehow. Of course that domino'd into other changes since suddenly the Giovanni and Lasombra had identical powersets and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T16:10:34-07:00","id":1484242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484239#post1484239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably worth noting oblivion theoretically covers mortis of the clan cappadocian whose discipline powers where comparatively neutral if grim compared to their giovanni successors and historically cappadocians where one of the less awful clans, then again I don't think it's possible to simulate mortis with Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It theoretically covers Mortis, Thanatosis, Deimos and Nihilistics. They all fit the same bill to some degree, less awful Disciplines from less awful clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T16:15:02-07:00","id":1484243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484242#post1484242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It theoretically covers Mortis, Thanatosis, Deimos and Nihilistics. They all fit the same bill to some degree, less awful Disciplines from less awful clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they combined all of them under the death magic umbrella, it provided an interesting subtext to the giovanni that the sinister nature of giovanni necromancy was cultural rather than inherent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T16:46:29-07:00","id":1484244,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they could\u2019ve served Obtenebration better by making it a series of Potence (+Obfuscate?) Amalgams. And leave Abyss Mysticism as (out-of-Clan-but-still-)Lasombra-flavored Necromancy, one that focuses on the deep Tempest realms itself more than its inhabitants and visitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T17:26:59-07:00","id":1484248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484244#post1484244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they could\u2019ve served Obtenebration better by making it a series of Potence (+Obfuscate?) Amalgams. And leave Abyss Mysticism as (out-of-Clan-but-still-)Lasombra-flavored Necromancy, one that focuses on the deep Tempest realms itself more than its inhabitants and visitors.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would've been certainly better if they had applied the Stain effect or some other consequence to the specific Abyss Mysticism-like effects instead of a blanket rule for everything with a Rousing check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T17:29:25-07:00","id":1484249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484244#post1484244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they could\u2019ve served Obtenebration better by making it a series of Potence (+Obfuscate?) Amalgams. And leave Abyss Mysticism as (out-of-Clan-but-still-)Lasombra-flavored Necromancy, one that focuses on the deep Tempest realms itself more than its inhabitants and visitors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't have worked. Obfuscate focuses on the manipulation of one's perceptions in V5. Making Obtenebration into an Obfuscate amalgam makes little sense in that context. If anything, it would work best as a group of Blood Sorcery powers. That said if they did that, 4 separate clans would have Blood Sorcery as an in-clan option. Also, because of the no unique disciplines rule, they couldn't make Obtenebration or Necromancy their own unique disciplines separately.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think they did what they had to do. They had to make a discipline that could fit with both a Clan of Shadows and a Clan of Death. So? Make a discipline based off the idea of entropy itself. It works! To bad they also had to make them on par with other powers in the game. I don't get why developers do this! They add a dangerous cost that could spell the end of a character if they use a set of powers, and immediately make powers the same level as other powers in the game.<br /> <br /> <i><b>It'S jUsT fOr FlAvOr!</b></i> No! Don't do it! If you add a sever cost of some kind, you make that power stronger in some way! Not only that, but other disciplines can do things some Oblivion powers can, but better! Wanna get rid of a body? Blood Sorcery can melt nonliving material. Guess what a corpse counts as! Wanna see in the dark? Protean and Auspex do it better. Yeah, but Oblivion can see ghosts at the same time! Auspex can do that and then some. Wanna hide better? Obfuscate...just obfuscate...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T17:39:24-07:00","id":1484250,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd have just binned the no unique discipline rule, it serves no practical purpose and wasn't even really formalised until supplementary works came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T18:23:40-07:00","id":1484251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484249#post1484249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I think they did what they had to do. They had to make a discipline that could fit with both a Clan of Shadows and a Clan of Death. So? Make a discipline based off the idea of entropy itself. It works! To bad they also had to make them on par with other powers in the game. I don't get why developers do this! They add a dangerous cost that could spell the end of a character if they use a set of powers, and immediately make powers the same level as other powers in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think with all the Paths and takes added to Necromancy over the years, it didn't really needed this change to work as a standalone broad Discipline. The only reason it would even seem to be so at a first glance was the coalescing of all Necromancers under Hecata, which is a debatable move. Not bad, imo, but they could have Hecata and Giovanni as distinct things and I think it would work better and make space for Necromancy to see more use (even because most of those other bloodlines never had such a compunction of not teaching outsiders).<br /> <br /> Obfuscate maybe not, but Obtenebration itself would work perfectly fine as just amalgam powers, not even many, one or two. One to control/materialize shadows, one to turn into shadows. Even in its original form, while strong and fun, it is thematically very repetitive, so it would work fine just as Dementation works as a single Amalgam for Dominate. We would just have to consider what other Discipline give the Lasombra to combine with Potence for this. I get why Obfuscate seems fitting, but it has always been about affecting perception, not light, even before V5. Dominate would make for a weird but maybe fitting choice as it literally &quot;commands&quot; shadows. From the perspective of the power itself and its common effects I would say Protean, Although Auspex may cover the ide of &quot;perceiving the Abyss&quot; to reach it. Finally, going through the route of this being a physical manifestation of some inner aspect, it could be Fortitude.<br /> <br /> Heck, just the darkness tentacles could be a standalone Potence power.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;costly-but-powerful&quot; aspect, that was what Abyss Mysticism was for, and I think it works really well either as Blood Magic, or as Necromancy, either as distinct powers and rituals or amalgams. Just by making it outside the primary in-clans (which it already was), it is far easier to make something more flavorful and less balanced in power level due to the concept. Again, while it was not really a planned design, just a happy accident, by divorcing AM from regular Obtenebration and letting the basic clan work as a normal one, they nailed it in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T01:51:31-07:00","id":1484272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1483997#post1483997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The main reason Oblivion likely gives a stain is the popular depiction of Necromancy.<br /> <br /> \u200bNecromancy is almost always seen as evil in popular media. This comes from years of several different cultures and beliefs dictating it as such..</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as the WoD has always been more pop-culture than folklore, it's actually done pretty well in terms of adapting real world belief systems concerning magical practices: Hermetic Tremere, Dur-An-Ki, Ahku, awesome supplement books like the thaumaturgy trilogy.... As much as Anarchs like to joke about it, magic in WoD was really set apart from DnD magic. Alchemy took inspiration from the real world: a science-mystic practice geared around changing one material to another or creating the perfect medicine and perfecting the mind and body beyond ordinary means. It very much avoided the so-commonly adopted DnD simplism of alchemy: making potions for temporary effects. And yet, that's where we are now with TBA. So as much evil necromancy fits the trend, that doesn't mean it fits the series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T04:14:33-07:00","id":1484282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484226#post1484226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an implication behind all this: the implication that your humanity is actually your soul, and not just a representation of your psychological resistance to berzerker hunger and rage. The force behind Oblivion literally eats your soul bit at a time. The idea of a soul eating discipline is...familiar...to those of us who played earlier editions, and I didn't like it the last time.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm comfortable with the idea that someone with Humanity 8 literally has a bigger soul than someone with Humanity 7. I've always treated that number as representing something psychological, a unique form of insanity that gradually overcomes vampires because their human brains are not designed to deal with berzerker urges. But things like this strongly imply that, nah, it's not a form of insanity: your soul literally shrinks over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. But V5 is no clearer on what Humanity is than earlier editions. It sort of wants to be VTR2e's Humanity (a type of Integrity), but then scrubs all the rules that establish that, ties it into morals again (Convictions, Tenets), and makes it about remorse and Stains rather than detachment and breaking points.<br /> <br /> This is one such muddled element in the mix. The idea behind it could be that Oblivion causes Stains because it has a deadening/detaching quality that makes you less human rather than less humane. And I think that's what it's going for, rather than that it eats your soul.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it's all a bit muddled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T09:01:56-07:00","id":1484289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484282#post1484282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly. But V5 is no clearer on what Humanity is than earlier editions. It sort of wants to be VTR2e's Humanity (a type of Integrity), but then scrubs all the rules that establish that, ties it into morals again (Convictions, Tenets), and makes it about remorse and Stains rather than detachment and breaking points.<br /> <br /> This is one such muddled element in the mix. The idea behind it could be that Oblivion causes Stains because it has a deadening/detaching quality that makes you less human rather than less humane. And I think that's what it's going for, rather than that it eats your soul.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it's all a bit muddled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want Oblivion to succeed Cr\u00faac, but what that means does depend on the nature of &quot;Humanity&quot; and it offers less reward for more frequent, but diminishing, risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T20:45:42-07:00","id":1484326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484211#post1484211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that the chance for losing Humanity when you use an Oblivion power is not all that high. It's a 1 in 5 chance for getting a stain, sure, but you get to make a remorse roll at the end of every session. The lower the character's humanity, the more likely they're going to pass the remorse roll. So yeah, an oblivion user is probably not going to stay at Humanity 7, but once they drop down to Humanity 5 or so, the chance of losing more gets pretty small.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, in games I played in V5, many ST's would not allow a remorse roll unless you had scenes RP'ing the remorse. So I think the one time I played a Lasombra that used higher level powers, I went from Humanity 6 to a Wight in 3 sessions, as I refused to RP remorse and told the ST &quot;Fuck it I'll lower humanity&quot; each time.<br /> <br /> Why would a Lasombra feel remorse for anything, remorse is for the weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18512-uriel","name":"uriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T21:35:51-07:00","id":1484329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>uriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484326#post1484326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a Lasombra feel remorse for anything, remorse is for the weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're still people and there's a long way between believing you shouldn't feel something and you actually not feeling it. And this is kind of the point with Humanity and any game that embraces its rule.<br /> <br /> It is also the reason why Paths exist, in more than one sense, but since there's no official rule for Paths, we're all stuck with Humanity in official rules for V5.<br /> <br /> To be honest, while forcing scenes to apply a necessary rule is a jerk move by the ST, I think that simply refusing to play along with the proposal of the chronicle is a jerk move, too. You can talk to the ST beforehand if you want to explore such a character concept, you can and should suggest other takes on Humanity if you think the RAW won't work for the themes and mood of the chronicle, and if you want to explore the descent of such a character into wightdom and everyone is ok with the idea at the table, go for it. But if you simply refused to play along the themes the ST wanted to explore, then you could have made a favor for everyone involved and simply not played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T02:31:21-07:00","id":1484339,"title":"","content":"As a veteran Lasombra player I can tell you they feel remorse. <br /> Knowing that, with every other character being less than half as capable as you, it's near impossible to reach the perfection you individually reach when part of such a group, and as any self respecting Lasombra knows; Anything less than perfect is a shameful stain. Even when you do pull everything off to your standard of perfection, the fools are too ignorant to appreciate your genius. *fiddles with his shadow* <br /> <br /> He's right though. Needing to &quot;RP&quot; remorse is pretty fucking stupid. Normal, high functioning people don't create a melodramatic monologue when they feel guilt. Remorse response can be anywhere between -I sit still and stay silent and think about what I did- and -I crack bad jokes and make a fool of myself because I'm not really sure how to cope in this situation-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T02:40:53-07:00","id":1484340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>uriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484326#post1484326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would a Lasombra feel remorse for anything, remorse is for the weak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lasombra are as emotionally complex as anyone else, it's worth noting the clan has a historical tendancy to rationalise their conduct.<br /> <br /> I've only played one who didn't really feel remorse for hid actions and he instead tempered his awfulness with a sense of honour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T02:52:34-07:00","id":1484342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484339#post1484339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's right though. Needing to &quot;RP&quot; remorse is pretty fucking stupid. Normal, high functioning people don't create a melodramatic monologue when they feel guilt. Remorse response can be anywhere between -I sit still and stay silent and think about what I did- and -I crack bad jokes and make a fool of myself because I'm not really sure how to cope in this situation-</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule I only tend to make you play through your first murder and level one sins, since both are pretty dramatic. I don't expect a speech and I tend to hold of the roll until things are calm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T04:53:20-07:00","id":1484347,"title":"","content":"Remorse checks makes sense if thought of as rationalization as well, besides just remorse. Things like &quot;But they deserved it&quot; or &quot;I did what I had to do&quot;, while losing Humanity would be accepting it, &quot;So what?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though now that I think of it, rationalizing the shitty stuff you did, means you feel remorseful for them, otherwise you wouldn't bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T08:11:29-07:00","id":1484358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484347#post1484347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remorse checks makes sense if thought of as rationalization as well, besides just remorse. Things like &quot;But they deserved it&quot; or &quot;I did what I had to do&quot;, while losing Humanity would be accepting it, &quot;So what?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though now that I think of it, rationalizing the shitty stuff you did, means you feel remorseful for them, otherwise you wouldn't bother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. Rationalisation is what you don't want to do. It's the unhealthy response to what you've done, as opposed to remorse.<br /> <br /> When you rationalise things, you're trying to stop the cognitive dissonance of, 'I'm a good person so how come I did a bad thing?' So you start making excuses for the things you do, making it easier to keep doing them.<br /> <br /> You change the above statement to, 'I'm a good person and I was right because...' or 'I'm a good person and what I did doesn't matter because...'<br /> <br /> Essentially, you're deluding yourself that the line isn't here (killing is bad), it's over there (killing is only bad if it's a good person). <br /> <br /> You keep doing that until the line makes no sense (killing is okay if I wear my purple hat while I do it) or doesn't exist (killing is okay).<br /> <br /> And that's when you become so far removed from humanity that you're a monster and either don't realise it or you don't care.<br /> <br /> Remorse is thinking, 'I'm [trying to be] a good person but I killed someone. Therefore, I won't kill anyone ever again and I'll make amends, so I can stay [trying to be] a good person.' <br /> <br /> It's supposed to stop you from rationalising the behaviour as acceptable. It reasserts the line (killing is always bad, regardless) rather than moving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-18-2022, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T09:13:41-07:00","id":1484361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484339#post1484339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's right though. Needing to &quot;RP&quot; remorse is pretty fucking stupid. Normal, high functioning people don't create a melodramatic monologue when they feel guilt. Remorse response can be anywhere between -I sit still and stay silent and think about what I did- and -I crack bad jokes and make a fool of myself because I'm not really sure how to cope in this situation-</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but his reasoning isn't.<br /> <br /> Demanding such a scene is, indeed, pretty stupid, though.<br /> <br /> Sometimes as an ST I just ask the player how the PC feels or cope, or I describe the feeling in general and let them decide how they externalize and deal with that, if I feel confident and it is interesting at the moment, which usually means the first time of a new character or some dramatic session. But requiring lengthy remorse monologues? Like, what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484358#post1484358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no. Rationalisation is what you don't want to do. It's the unhealthy response to what you've done, as opposed to remorse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a> is right here.<br /> <br /> Humanity in VtM isn't about believing in a certain code or having a healthy response (it isn't mental health exactly). It is about <i>feelings</i>. How do you deal with your feelings, or lack thereof, is another matter (albeit still a pretty relevant one for the character). You can have a character that pretty much doesn't think killing is ever justifiable, yet are below the Humanity rating (for V20, for example) to feel about murder. If they commit a murder they may feel a little bad for going against their belief, but it is more abstract, not a response to the fact they actually ended a life. Likewise, you can have a character that whose beliefs completely justify murder in a lot of circumstances, yet it doesn't mean actually doing it became emotionally easy.<br /> <br /> In V5 it is about the feelings become gradually more muted instead of things slipping in or out of the list, which may be a better or worse take for it depending on the character and the Chronicle Tenets, but the baseline is still the same. Convictions may help with this notion as they may signify situations where your belief in the justification is strong enough to help you cope emotionally. But otherwise it is about emotions, not beliefs, and as such rationalization is an indirect factor.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you rationalize it may also mean you're more likely to do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T09:17:56-07:00","id":1484362,"title":"","content":"Rationalization being a valid way to RP remorse checks makes sense when you take Convictions into account and how they stop you from accruing stains.<br /> <br /> V5's humanity system suffers from being too tied to old fluff tbh, it can have unhealthy coping mechanisms, as it ends mostly being a meter of Beast Control.<br /> <br /> Rationalizing your awful actions at least means you are in control, you did stuff because (you believe) it was necessary, with failing meaning you succumb to self-loathing and accept that what you did was bad, and that's just who you are.<br /> <br /> So A. You regret what you did or B. You lie to yourself that you didn't so much bad shit or some other excuse, because otherwise the guilt is too much.<br /> <br /> As opposed to C. You blatantly accept it, it is just how things are now. or D. You can't justify it, instead falling into self-loathing and giving space to the Beast as you weaken.<br /> <br /> Or countless other ways.<br /> <br /> At the end, I prefer that players personalize how their characters deal with Remorse checks, over forcing characters to behave in certain ways. <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484361#post1484361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if you rationalize it may also mean you're more likely to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if your are more likely to do it again, there'll eventually be a point where you fail and can't justify it anymore, therefore losing humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":".  Added a reply 06-18-2022, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T17:51:56-07:00","id":1484404,"title":"","content":"I agree that it is a terrible mechanic. Why have the Lasombra join the Camarilla if they're not meant to be played?<br /> <br /> It's not like they're not already going to be Low Humanity vampires for the ACTUAL evil shit they do rather than turning Oblivion into the Dark Side of the Force or One Ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T18:16:42-07:00","id":1484405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484404#post1484404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it is a terrible mechanic. Why have the Lasombra join the Camarilla if they're not meant to be played?<br /> <br /> It's not like they're not already going to be Low Humanity vampires for the ACTUAL evil shit they do rather than turning Oblivion into the Dark Side of the Force or One Ring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be more okay with it if they had rules for Paths and if the assumption was that most Lasombra (and Hecata) ended up on a Path in order to deal with the Humanity loss that would eventually come from using their signature Discipline. But there are no rules for Paths so all playable Lasombra and Hecata will be on Humanity. And sure, for many players the odds will be on their side and they'll be able to use their in-clan Discipline with no real issues. But some players will inevitably end up being unlucky, will have bad roles, and will lose their Humanity very quickly. And for those players, losing character stats because they wanted to use the Discipline they invested experience into will likely not be a terribly fun time.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Not arguing with you or anything. Just that your comment jumpstarted something on my end that I've thought about a few times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-18-2022, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T23:28:22-07:00","id":1484417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484361#post1484361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but his reasoning isn't.<br /> <br /> Demanding such a scene is, indeed, pretty stupid, though.<br /> <br /> Sometimes as an ST I just ask the player how the PC feels or cope, or I describe the feeling in general and let them decide how they externalize and deal with that, if I feel confident and it is interesting at the moment, which usually means the first time of a new character or some dramatic session. But requiring lengthy remorse monologues? Like, what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's obnoxious. You can't really RP that stuff, beyond letting it flavour some of the character's actions. Though making amends should be grounds for buying up Humanity again (see V20DA for a system for that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a> is right here.<br /> <br /> Humanity in VtM isn't about believing in a certain code or having a healthy response (it isn't mental health exactly). It is about <i>feelings</i>. How do you deal with your feelings, or lack thereof, is another matter (albeit still a pretty relevant one for the character). You can have a character that pretty much doesn't think killing is ever justifiable, yet are below the Humanity rating (for V20, for example) to feel about murder. If they commit a murder they may feel a little bad for going against their belief, but it is more abstract, not a response to the fact they actually ended a life. Likewise, you can have a character that whose beliefs completely justify murder in a lot of circumstances, yet it doesn't mean actually doing it became emotionally easy.<br /> <br /> In V5 it is about the feelings become gradually more muted instead of things slipping in or out of the list, which may be a better or worse take for it depending on the character and the Chronicle Tenets, but the baseline is still the same. Convictions may help with this notion as they may signify situations where your belief in the justification is strong enough to help you cope emotionally. But otherwise it is about emotions, not beliefs, and as such rationalization is an indirect factor.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you rationalize it may also mean you're more likely to do it again. </div> </div> </div>So, checking the text again, you're both right RAW. V20 and Revised talk about the degeneration roll as 'he feels enough remorse or somehow justifies it to himself', and I think this is symptomatic of how Humanity has been poorly articulated throughout the game (even in V5).<br /> <br /> In my view, as soon as you start saying killing is okay in some circumstances, you've started down the slippery slope of allowing killing. And the downward spiral of Humanity is supposed to, at least in part, portray that slippery slope, until you reach the point at which killing is commonplace.<br /> <br /> Paths are different. But having a strong Conscience suggests a person should be feeling remorse, not rationalising (which is the logical ego overriding the superego, and therefore overriding Conscience).<br /> <br /> That's why I much prefer VTR2e's breaking points and detachment as a system, to be honest. It completely sidesteps the quagmire. I guess we also shouldn't expect too much logic from an RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-19-2022, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T06:16:42-07:00","id":1484420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484405#post1484405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be more okay with it if they had rules for Paths and if the assumption was that most Lasombra (and Hecata) ended up on a Path in order to deal with the Humanity loss that would eventually come from using their signature Discipline. But there are no rules for Paths so all playable Lasombra and Hecata will be on Humanity. And sure, for many players the odds will be on their side and they'll be able to use their in-clan Discipline with no real issues. But some players will inevitably end up being unlucky, will have bad roles, and will lose their Humanity very quickly. And for those players, losing character stats because they wanted to use the Discipline they invested experience into will likely not be a terribly fun time.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Not arguing with you or anything. Just that your comment jumpstarted something on my end that I've thought about a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is just one of the times I flat out disagree with an OPP decision.<br /> <br /> Though I wouldn't be surprised if this came down from on high.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T02:04:36-07:00","id":1484488,"title":"","content":"They have rules for Paths. Right in the corebook.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V5 Core p.172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Convictions<br /> <br /> Each character begins with one to three Convictions: human values they attempt to uphold even after death.<br /> <br /> The specifics of these Convictions are up to the player. <i><u><b>They might reflect</b></u></i> a religious code, a personal ethical core, <i><u><b>a vampiric path</b></u></i>, or just things the character does or balks at doing without ever<br /> really considering their philosophical weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just pick something like &quot;Never turn away from the Abyss&quot; as one of your Convictions and tank that 1 Stain every time. Not that the stain rule should be there, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T03:01:19-07:00","id":1484491,"title":"","content":"It is not only worthless but also manages to make a whole clan worthless by fusing what used to be necromancy with Obtenebration<br /> <br /> The result is that now the lasombra and the giovanni/hecata have the same spread but the LaSombra who were one of the fan favourite clans are now the bad choice and also have a clan curse that makes them almost unplayable due to them being unable to properly use tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T03:04:11-07:00","id":1484492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484420#post1484420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is just one of the times I flat out disagree with an OPP decision.<br /> <br /> Though I wouldn't be surprised if this came down from on high.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its always felt more like an anachronistic development idea which should have been nixed early on. A lot of v5's more controversial ideas feel like something which needed more development or was someone's pet idea which no one considered how it would work in the wild.<br /> Heceta and lasombra's developement in v5 does feel railroaded by some mandate for example the frankly absurd fusion of necromancy and obtenerbration but I'm more inclined to chalk oblivion negative side effects as a design gaffe rather than some calculated decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T11:06:03-07:00","id":1484520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484488#post1484488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have rules for Paths. Right in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just pick something like &quot;Never turn away from the Abyss&quot; as one of your Convictions and tank that 1 Stain every time. Not that the stain rule should be there, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Already mentioned in a previous post that Convictions by RAW only negate stains you get from breaking Chronicle Tenets. Unless your ST says otherwise, this would not work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T11:56:55-07:00","id":1484527,"title":"","content":"And, without even more house rules, if you do have a Conviction that would negate the Oblivion Stains, and your ST lets it apply, you have to maintain a Touchstone that specifically embodies that Conviction for you; which grows increasingly hard to justify the more supernatural/esoteric the Conviction is.<br /> <br /> Odds are (again without even more house rules) that such a Conviction is just stalling things rather than truly negating them, with a giant Stain hit when that dam finally breaks on top of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T22:29:42-07:00","id":1484579,"title":"","content":"Yes, the ability of both Convictions and Chronicle Tenets to work as Path-like <b><u>is</u></b> one of the good things about V5. But it only goes so far to really address the problem. As far as Paths go, it works well for some chronicles and not at all at others. Then you have Touchstones and things get weirder if you step outside very limited boundaries.<br /> <br /> And even if you house-rule that Convictions can affect Oblivion Stains and that you don't need a human Touchstone for it, this &quot;solution&quot; is basically saying that you have to dedicate one of your limited three Convictions just to use your in-clan Discipline that you bought. It patches, but do not actually solves the underlying problems.<br /> <br /> Not to say that just house-ruling that Oblivion does not cause Stains is a simpler solution that actually solves it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T03:51:46-07:00","id":1484599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484492#post1484492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecata and lasombra's developement in v5 does feel railroaded by some mandate for example the frankly absurd fusion of necromancy and obtenerbration but I'm more inclined to chalk oblivion negative side effects as a design gaffe rather than some calculated decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that these two very different disciplines were stitched together in order to simplify the cosmology and reduce the number of alternate dimensions out there. It's probably the brainchild of whichever developer wanted umbral travel to be really hard for werewolves in W5. All of this cracking down on the Umbra has hilarious implications for M5 as well, if that game manages to happen before the World of Darkness IP's get sold again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T04:21:26-07:00","id":1484600,"title":"","content":"Except that the whole Abyssal Mysticism thing never really involved going to the Umbra. It was just a rationale of where Obtenebration's shadows really came from to explain all the things they could do that don't really make sense. You don't need there to be an Umbra, with the Abyss Realm, for Obtenebration or Abyssal Mysticism to work as they do in VtM... it was just a connection that was cool to have for crossover material.<br /> <br /> The simplest explanation is that they wanted to keep some avenue of Abyssal Mysticism open in V5, but didn't want to put Obtenebration into Blood Sorcery, so they combined it with Necromancy into Oblivion instead. Lasombra can, in theory access Ceremonies so they keep some of that mystic flavor without having three Clans with Blood Sorcery as in-Clan.<br /> <br /> If you dump Abyssal Mysticism, it's much much easier to make a few Obtenebration inspired new Obfuscate Powers/Amalgams and call it a day. No connection to another Realm, no overloaded Oblivion, etc. Oblivion only makes sense as it currently stands if it was designed to keep it connected to another dimension. It's not really simplifying anything when the Underworld was already part of the larger Umbra in the grand WoD cosmology to move the Abyss from the Near Umbra to the Dark Umbra instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T06:59:37-07:00","id":1484603,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate wouldn't rationalise Obtenebration. It kind of works for moving shadows or making the room dark and muffled, but not for shadow grappling, suffocation, transformation or teleportation. It needs some sort of fantasy field of physics, whether that's worldly or not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T07:51:37-07:00","id":1484607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484404#post1484404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it is a terrible mechanic. Why have the Lasombra join the Camarilla if they're not meant to be played?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Rad theory: Many of the v5 writers don't think the Camarilla should be played, so unplayable, written-into-a-corner Lasombra fits perfectly with this mindset. <br /> <br /> <br /> Even if Oblivion wasn't bad-wrong-dark-arts, the Lasombra in this edition have lost their desirability to Lasombra players. The new clan weakness and the terms and conditions they've agreed to to join the Camarilla very much serve to make impotent and undermine a clan that has always been about domineering and overbearing strength. I'll admit it: RPing your average lasombra well can come off pretty toxic at times, so I can kinda understand why they want to discourage the clan for player use and have them exclusively used for cartoon villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T11:20:15-07:00","id":1484628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484607#post1484607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rad theory: Many of the v5 writers don't think the Camarilla should be played, so unplayable, written-into-a-corner Lasombra fits perfectly with this mindset. <br /> <br /> <br /> Even if Oblivion wasn't bad-wrong-dark-arts, the Lasombra in this edition have lost their desirability to Lasombra players. The new clan weakness and the terms and conditions they've agreed to to join the Camarilla very much serve to make impotent and undermine a clan that has always been about domineering and overbearing strength. I'll admit it: RPing your average lasombra well can come off pretty toxic at times, so I can kinda understand why they want to discourage the clan for player use and have them exclusively used for cartoon villains.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got the impression it was more about discouraging Sabbat play than anything, much like sudden surge in anarch tzmisce. Lasombra are ultimately really cool and people want to play them but v5 doesn't want you playing Sabbat so parawolf 'solved' this issue by having them defect but didn't really consider how this would even work or make the lasombra look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-21-2022, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T11:35:36-07:00","id":1484630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484607#post1484607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rad theory: Many of the v5 writers don't think the Camarilla should be played, so unplayable, written-into-a-corner Lasombra fits perfectly with this mindset.<br /> <br /> Even if Oblivion wasn't bad-wrong-dark-arts, the Lasombra in this edition have lost their desirability to Lasombra players. The new clan weakness and the terms and conditions they've agreed to to join the Camarilla very much serve to make impotent and undermine a clan that has always been about domineering and overbearing strength. I'll admit it: RPing your average lasombra well can come off pretty toxic at times, so I can kinda understand why they want to discourage the clan for player use and have them exclusively used for cartoon villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm going to say that is pretty silly.<br /> <br /> I mean, we don't have to speculate because I think it was Matthew Dawkins who actually proposed the Lasombra joining the Camarilla and he gave his reasons.<br /> <br /> Which was....make it easier to play Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484628#post1484628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the impression it was more about discouraging Sabbat play than anything, much like sudden surge in anarch tzmisce. Lasombra are ultimately really cool and people want to play them but v5 doesn't want you playing Sabbat so parawolf 'solved' this issue by having them defect but didn't really consider how this would even work or make the lasombra look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they were discouraging Sabbat play so much as opening up more options for other sects. Everyone can join any sect now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T12:14:09-07:00","id":1484636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484603#post1484603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obfuscate wouldn't rationalise Obtenebration. It kind of works for moving shadows or making the room dark and muffled, but not for shadow grappling, suffocation, transformation or teleportation. It needs some sort of fantasy field of physics, whether that's worldly or not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Amalgams are for. Obfuscate = shadow play, Obfuscate + Potence = imbue shadows with physical power so they can attack people. That's as much &quot;fantasy physics&quot; as goes into most Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The only real objection to Obfuscate + Potence is suddenly the Nosferatu can easily do it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484630#post1484630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they were discouraging Sabbat play so much as opening up more options for other sects. Everyone can join any sect now.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet... Sabbat V5 is out and we know how they feel about playable Sabbat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T13:31:48-07:00","id":1484642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484600#post1484600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest explanation is that they wanted to keep some avenue of Abyssal Mysticism open in V5, but didn't want to put Obtenebration into Blood Sorcery, so they combined it with Necromancy into Oblivion instead. Lasombra can, in theory access Ceremonies so they keep some of that mystic flavor without having three Clans with Blood Sorcery as in-Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that Abyss Mysticism has always been one of those hard-to-get powers that aren't really in-clan for anyone. The Lasombra had a monopoly on it, but it was actually hard and rare among them (and seriously, even without this it was niche enough that I rarely considered it for my Lasombra characters anyway). Personally I think that it being modeled as Blood Sorcery would work perfectly.<br /> <br /> My take is, indeed, that they kind of focused too much on the other dimension concept. Which is silly, as tying Obtenebration to the Daark Umbra does not really help with its themes, and the Abyss...<br /> <br /> Here the thing is, &quot;the Abyss&quot; is one of the confusing bits in the lore that really work being confusing, as each iteration of the concept is ultimately a very simple phenomenon that can be used in several distinct ways, so they don't need definitive answers to work fine and you can give any answer to use them in novel ways in your game.<br /> <br /> We have a total of four &quot;Abysses&quot; in the setting: the Near Umbra Realm of Depression linked to Harano, the Dark Umbra alternate name to the Tempest, the undisclosed out-of-reality realm of the Fallen and the Dark, Fluid and Lovecraftian realm of Abyss Mysticism. They're all dark places where perception is skewed or impossible, are particularly hard for most splats to even consider entrance, and most give exactly zero confirmed reasons for you to go there. Like, two of them are quite possibly just useless empty space anyway, and one is arguably only filled with formless shadows that become something relevant because of the magic getting them out of there.<br /> <br /> Linking the two in Oblivion is a clear (albeit possibly wrong) message that they want to make at least two Abysses into one, but for what? It adds nothing, doesn't explain any meaningful mystery, and still doesn't make sense for the mechanic of Stains. Unless they're also intending to make one of the other Abysses be in this unified thing, then it may be either a leakage of Torment or Harano.<br /> <br /> So they're maybe getting Stains because the Lasombra are being tainted by the powers of... Depression and/or PTSD. G-reat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484607#post1484607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rad theory: Many of the v5 writers don't think the Camarilla should be played, so unplayable, written-into-a-corner Lasombra fits perfectly with this mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much make the Camarilla unplayable, but make it weak and crippling angst-intense. Only Anarchs can be moderate-angst to angst-free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484628#post1484628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression it was more about discouraging Sabbat play than anything,</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484630#post1484630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they were discouraging Sabbat play so much as opening up more options for other sects. Everyone can join any sect now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabbat-wise they're not discouraging since they outright forbid it, you need to house-rule to even try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T13:48:52-07:00","id":1484644,"title":"","content":"What are themes of Obtenebration in the absence of any Abysses? No Abyss is needed for Khaibit Obtenebration, but at they have something connecting to themselves and the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T13:57:36-07:00","id":1484645,"title":"","content":"Besides the Khaibit having a power called Obetenebration, that's almost an apples and oranges thing because the name was part of VtR 1e's shout outs/Easter eggs to VtM stuff. The Khaibit are vampires that specialize in hunting otherworldly entities (which is important in VtR since very few vampires are good at that, and the CofD has a much more unified ephemeral entities system).<br /> <br /> The themes of Obtenebration in VtM, outside of the Abyss, is pretty simple: creepy shadow powers. The whole Abyss thing was just some fluff until later in VtM as it is. For 1e and (IIRC all, but I might be forgetting a later book) 2e Obtenebration was just super shadow manipulation with some weird rumors about the shadows connecting to some otherworldly Realm rather than just being the manipulation of normal shadows. It wasn't until later that Abyssal Mysticism became a real thing with mechanics that really solidified that the power did in fact connect to some greater darkness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:00:42-07:00","id":1484647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484642#post1484642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sabbat-wise they're not discouraging since they outright forbid it, you need to house-rule to even try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a Sabbat player, yes it sucks.<br /> <br /> My hope is that Onyx Path will again be the guys to fix it. Make a Blood Cult called The Children of Caine or Sword of Nod and have it be a Sabbat off-shoot that allows it to be the &quot;real&quot; Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I do think Lasombra Anarchs and Tzimisce Camarilla are awesome, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:25:33-07:00","id":1484650,"title":"","content":"And they've been a thing for a while now. V5 didn't make them possible, it made them less rare. And you can't really separate out making it less rare to see more members of Clans in Sects the &quot;main&quot; Clan isn't well represented in, from the reduction of the Sabbat from a playable state. We only have more Lasombra and Tzimisce prominently out in other Sects in V5 because V5 took a massive ax to the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:56:22-07:00","id":1484654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484642#post1484642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sabbat-wise they're not discouraging since they outright forbid it, you need to house-rule to even try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I should have clarified the defection of the lasombra is designed to mitigate the obvious issue of not being able to play Sabbat. Sweaten the pill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-21-2022, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T23:35:29-07:00","id":1484674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484644#post1484644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are themes of Obtenebration in the absence of any Abysses? No Abyss is needed for Khaibit Obtenebration, but at they have something connecting to themselves and the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme is &quot;Lasombra are creepy&quot;, which is its theme with or without the Abyss and the legend that Obtenebration comes from there (even Abyss Mysticism does not confirms with complete certainty that normal Obtenebration has anything to do with the place).<br /> <br /> It has never been any other theme, and as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> points out it wasn't even an actual thing for a long time. And the Lasombra aren't considered particularly evil because they deal with it, it is just an aftereffect of them being creepy. Even their Ante was ultimately just power-hungry and creepy instead of really mysterious and hard to understand, more like an edgy bully than anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484647#post1484647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hope is that Onyx Path will again be the guys to fix it. Make a Blood Cult called The Children of Caine or Sword of Nod and have it be a Sabbat off-shoot that allows it to be the &quot;real&quot; Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I do think Lasombra Anarchs and Tzimisce Camarilla are awesome, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with both. Unfortunately it will take the goodwill of Paradox first, as they're clearly the ones that don't want Sabbat or Paths to happen, but I do hope that eventually they'll let OPP to come in and make it happen.<br /> <br /> Without Paths, though, those off-shoots would be really weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T04:06:47-07:00","id":1484688,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1484630]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, we don't have to speculate because I think it was Matthew Dawkins who actually proposed the Lasombra joining the Camarilla and he gave his reasons. </div> </div> </div>Don't namedrop authors. It's pretty easy to criticise work, but it becomes nasty when you throw the author's name in. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which was....make it easier to play Lasombra. </div> </div> </div>And yet, the conditions the Lasombra agreed upon make it considerably harder (impossible) to play a Lasombra in the Camarilla. (and also the main appeal of the lasombra has been curtailed and so on and so forth...) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think they were discouraging Sabbat play so much as opening up more options for other sects. Everyone can join any sect now. </div> </div> </div>1-But they didn't do that. They cut the Brujah out of the Cam's favoured member club. All the necromancers have been press-ganged into the Hecata.. and so on and so forth. <br /> 2-Other than the Camarilla (which was friendly for pragmatic purposes) , sects were hostile to one-another and having many sects in a city/mixed coteries was a pretty bad idea. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T04:19:04-07:00","id":1484690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484674#post1484674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theme is &amp;quot;Lasombra are creepy&amp;quot;, which is its theme with or without the Abyss and the legend that Obtenebration comes from there (even Abyss Mysticism does not confirms with complete certainty that normal Obtenebration has anything to do with the place).<br /> <br /> It has never been any other theme, and as <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> points out it wasn't even an actual thing for a long time. And the Lasombra aren't considered particularly evil because they deal with it, it is just an aftereffect of them being creepy. Even their Ante was ultimately just power-hungry and creepy instead of really mysterious and hard to understand, more like an edgy bully than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with both. Unfortunately it will take the goodwill of Paradox first, as they're clearly the ones that don't want Sabbat or Paths to happen, but I do hope that eventually they'll let OPP to come in and make it happen.<br /> <br /> Without Paths, though, those off-shoots would be really weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think were going to be in for a wait for a Sabbat restoration in any context. I suspect the acid test is how w5/m5 does since they seem to be approaching from a simular angle to v5. Should they undersell or even tank Paradox may re consider their perspectives, if they do well it'll be seem as affirmation to stay the coarse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T10:16:20-07:00","id":1484709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484690#post1484690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think were going to be in for a wait for a Sabbat restoration in any context. I suspect the acid test is how w5/m5 does since they seem to be approaching from a simular angle to v5. Should they undersell or even tank Paradox may re consider their perspectives, if they do well it'll be seem as affirmation to stay the coarse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything I've heard about WTA leads me to conclude that it'll be an unmitigated disaster. But then again, V5 has it's fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T11:51:12-07:00","id":1484714,"title":"","content":"I think when discussion of the game ever supporting broader play options or going back on its design choices or what all have you happens, it has to be taken into account that ultimately Paradox did a pretty considerable marketing push as far as V5. They seem to have put in substantial funding for that and including avenues that haven't previously existed for the gameline, including a &quot;get popular internet tabletop people to do a liveplay, now that such things are how you sell your game&quot;, I don't really think they care too hard about the pre-existing fanbase at this point (unless fanbase is defined as &quot;really liked the Vampire 1e corebook and nothing much else&quot;). We're going to age out of the game inevitably (granted this may take a while considering VtM as it previously existed was publishing material right into the clearly ancient and disregardable before time of... 2018), and for the new customers they've brought in, V5 is the only vampire they know or will know going forward. The overall narrow playstyle and everything enforcing it, which includes things like Oblivion's &quot;you don't want to use your weird superpower that much, it will hose and punish you to do so&quot; mechanic become features thereby, not bugs. You can see this even from developer comments you can find online saying stuff ranging from that having a narrow take and potential for a game is actually good because Vampire should be like Pendragon, and that anyone who has a problem with that sort of thing can go play V20 if it bothers them so much (they say that last thing more politely and &quot;amiably&quot;, but they do say it).<br /> <br /> Which, sure, makes ironic its at times outright vengeful feeling osr-like push at the heart of it, and sure, that I dislike almost all of V5's design and setting choices makes that suck, but at the end of the day, it seems to be selling well enough just fine, it's brought in enough new people just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T15:04:40-07:00","id":1484728,"title":"","content":"I doubt they'd walk back on the focus on humanity, which is the crux of the issue. Playable Paths is contrary to that, and the Sabbat depends on those.<br /> <br /> Perhaps when they decide to do a new edition, but it works as it is and so I think changing it now would be a bad move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T16:59:25-07:00","id":1484730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484709#post1484709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything I've heard about WTA leads me to conclude that it'll be an unmitigated disaster. But then again, V5 has it's fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know there are a number of people unhappy with the Get of Fenris receiving the V5 Sabbat treatment. That's why my group won't be touching it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T17:07:33-07:00","id":1484731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484709#post1484709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything I've heard about WTA leads me to conclude that it'll be an unmitigated disaster. But then again, V5 has it's fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5 has certain merits and has a back to basics 91 approach which while flawed has a certain charm and merits. W5 is going to run into trouble because because its never really diverged from its origins. Its pretty simular across editions so its hard to justify the big shake up they're proposing outside of maybe improving combat and the issues with the pure tribes.<br /> <br /> More importantly it doesn't have the flagship status of vtm and they've cashed in a lot of fan goodwill from 20 so w5's position is a lot more shacky<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484730#post1484730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know there are a number of people unhappy with the Get of Fenris receiving the V5 Sabbat treatment. That's why my group won't be touching it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the overt antipathy towards get fans leaves me very cold. Between get and the sabbat I'm wondering who they're going to shaft next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-22-2022, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T17:41:08-07:00","id":1484733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484714#post1484714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think they care too hard about the pre-existing fanbase at this point</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably don't, and arguably shouldn't. If the game stands on its own, then our grognard hearts will just have to accept it.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, time still goes on, and they're still subject to it.<br /> <br /> Most of their mistakes as we perceive it are things that many others did in the past, and fans sooner or later reacted to. Think about Paths: in 1st ed core they didn't exist, an when they first appeared they were clearly meant to be just very crude justifications for the Sabbat, not really meant for a &quot;serious&quot; game. It was time, and the same fanbase that never saw it before, that demanded from them a more serious and nuanced work on Paths, and eventually the creation of Roads for DAV.<br /> <br /> As time goes on, their current fanbase will grow in their understanding of the rules and make more complex demands. Just as we did a long time ago, so we currently have several editions and in-edition variations instead of just 30 years of supplements to 1st Core. Maybe their future demands won't be the same we make. Maybe some will, as they <b>have</b> access to previous editions and may go for them between V5 publications, <i><b>as several forum members already did</b></i>. They're maybe not a majority, but a significant number of the people here began at V5, and this number is growing by the day without that keeping them out of V20 discussions.<br /> <br /> Either way, their mistakes will come to them sooner or later, as they did the people that designed RPGs for decades before them, including White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T19:17:28-07:00","id":1484743,"title":"","content":"Well I mean it's kinda already happened, hasn't it? I've been running V5 Sabbat games since shortly after I got a copy of Long Hard Road Out Of Hell. And the STV is full of other Sabbat supplements. It really didn't take the Sabbat community long at all to adapt to V5.<br /> <br /> Unlife uh finds uh finds a way, uh yes, finds a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T22:09:31-07:00","id":1484757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484731#post1484731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the overt antipathy towards get fans leaves me very cold. Between get and the sabbat I'm wondering who they're going to shaft next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere<br /> Brujah (or at least the half of them that don't lean left)<br /> Lasombra<br /> Get<br /> <br /> ...Probably the order of Hermes?<br /> <br /> ...All the asshole groups, basically. I think it's more than a little misguided to attack the &quot;problematic&quot; groups this way. Vampires and Werewolves are, in their entirety, problematic. It's a satire. That's what satires do. They hold up systemic ills and lampoon them for their faults. They're not supposed to write them off into a remote corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-23-2022, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T23:52:22-07:00","id":1484759,"title":"","content":"Satire does, however, need to be updated and revised over time to maintain relevance. People only read <i>A Modest Proposal</i> to study the art of satire, not because it's actually that great of a story for 2022. Now, that doesn't mean V5 did this update well, but it not being beholden to past iterations is essential to the satire elements of the game. Basically, satire alone isn't a defense of how things were, and thus how things should be.<br /> <br /> To try to keep this thread focused on VtM at least, the loss of playable Sabbat and making Oblivion needlessly punishing to play, isn't inherently good or bad. It needs to be analyzed in how it serves the satirical commentary of contemporary society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T03:34:13-07:00","id":1484763,"title":"","content":"Personally I got the impression the lack of sabbat play is a product of the idealisation of early/personal horror based vtm and the increased emphasis on the anarchs rather than any intrinsic social commentary. If their is a social context of the Sabbat and Sabbat players being....I want to use shunned but it seems too harsh? Its the fear of moral panic following the early incidents in v5's development. I know some people unironically think the Sabbat is a fascist : pinches Bridge of nose: so i can see why they might be gun shy. If there is a social commentary here it might be meta &quot;sabbat play is now unacceptable regardless of merit because of social issues.,&quot;<br /> <br /> I sincerly think oblivions punishing nature is a design gaffe. Someone thought it'd be cool but didn't think how it'd do on table. I genuinely don't it has anything going on beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-23-2022, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T04:41:59-07:00","id":1484765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484759#post1484759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satire does, however, need to be updated and revised over time to maintain relevance. People only read <i>A Modest Proposal</i> to study the art of satire, not because it's actually that great of a story for 2022. Now, that doesn't mean V5 did this update well, but it not being beholden to past iterations is essential to the satire elements of the game. Basically, satire alone isn't a defense of how things were, and thus how things should be.<br /> <br /> To try to keep this thread focused on VtM at least, the loss of playable Sabbat and making Oblivion needlessly punishing to play, isn't inherently good or bad. It needs to be analyzed in how it serves the satirical commentary of contemporary society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well no, as design choices go, VtM 5th maintaining its structural and thematic integrity mostly by attempted punitive measures and setting fire to various play options is inching close enough to the land of inherently bad you can see it without a telescope. It speaks to the level of assumed disdain for even its players people outside WoD gaming would lobby as a critique at it. &quot;If we let these rules support something other than our precious and artistic interpretation of how this game should play, you'll be doing it- gasp- wrong, therefore the game will actively work against the very idea.&quot; If you can't trust your players to enjoy your game in the way you want it to be without doing that, you kind of don't have a lot of respect for your players.<br /> <br /> Also considering things like entirely findable dev comments on &quot;we don't really want to do our world but darker anymore, our world is dark enough.&quot;, the satire thing is an increasingly thin patina over stuff (and also something that mostly served as a fig leaf in earlier editions). I've read across all the editions, and the idea of WoD as modern social satire has really only been there when really, really, really unsubtle, ala Pentex. It's otherwise one of those &quot;you've said that word so many times it has lost all meaning&quot; situations. There are exceptions, but if you eyeball the line as a whole, the energy and time and space put into the satire thing is not all that common. 40k has a better claim to being a satire based gameline than the WoD (and even they've increasingly ditched that idea).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T07:30:54-07:00","id":1484770,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go too far either way for pre-V5. There is satire, it just isn't the whole of the game. This is specially true as time goes on, because this is natural: the more time you expend in any fictional setting, the more this setting naturally deviates from original intentions and inspirations to pursue its own logical conclusions.<br /> <br /> But even if not always satirical, the WoD had always been commentary-friendly: it is our world but darker, isn't shy of having bad things and even letting you play those things, the authors tacitly accepted (to varying degrees) the idea that characters of every ideological leanings could and would exist and not always suffer the consequences for it they personally thought they should.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I completely agree that satire itself must be updated, and I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> didn't meant by that that ditching the Sabbat <b><u>was</u></b> a good idea, just that it must be analyzed from the right perspective. There are several valid reasons we discussed in the proper thread why it isn't a good idea, but the reason <i><b>isn't</b></i> just that the game should remain the same. Actually the Sabbat does need some update precisely for the reasons of updating satire, just not in the way it was done and definitely not by just ditching it.<br /> <br /> The idealization of 1st edition is a given at this point, and it has the same problem with idealization in general: it misses the mark far more than it realizes. It ignores 1st edition also had thematic contradictions, broad usage, not always had a clear idea of what it was doing, had good writing and bad writing, it was an inspiring amount of interesting ideas thrown together in a messy way and bad rules, by people that had artistic experience in the field, but no professional training or technical knowledge, because professional training and technical knowledge in writing RPGs weren't a thing at the time.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm not against ditching the whole &quot;Our World But Darker\u2122&quot; spiel, I've actually done this in my own games a long time ago. Our world but weirder? Sure, although our world can get pretty weird sometimes (I mean, aside from being pretty fucked up and sad for its many bad consequences and &quot;small&quot; tragedies, three years ago I would outright say that an invasion on Capitol just isn't credible if you're not running a Gehenna scenario, much less an invasion by a bunch of mostly incompetent lunatics). But changing this doesn't have to mean &quot;I want my WoD game to be a safer place where the bad people are easily recognized as such.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the Oblivion part of it... I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> is right. There certainly <b>is</b> an idea behind it, but by itself it was just a design gaffe. It happens. Whatever the intention was, the rule just failed at conveying it and working for the final product, and it isn't a particularly bad problem, just a small mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:10:41-07:00","id":1484789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484688#post1484688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't namedrop authors. It's pretty easy to criticise work, but it becomes nasty when you throw the author's name in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I criticize what I consider a great idea?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:17:25-07:00","id":1484790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484757#post1484757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere<br /> Brujah (or at least the half of them that don't lean left)<br /> Lasombra<br /> Get<br /> <br /> ...Probably the order of Hermes?<br /> <br /> ...All the asshole groups, basically. I think it's more than a little misguided to attack the &quot;problematic&quot; groups this way. Vampires and Werewolves are, in their entirety, problematic. It's a satire. That's what satires do. They hold up systemic ills and lampoon them for their faults. They're not supposed to write them off into a remote corner.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few points:<br /> <br /> 1. The Tremere only lost the Council of Seven and that has suck all to do with the average Tremere character unless they're living in the Vienna chantry for some reason. The Tremere loyalists have their own faction while there's multiple other houses.<br /> <br /> 2. The Hellenistic Brujah were established in the same book as them getting kicked out of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 3. The Lasombra have their own video game and a massively much-larger portion of the fanbase than they did before.<br /> <br /> 4. We don't know what the situation with the Get is until the book comes out. The visual novel that vilified the Get actually made it clear that they were NOT Nazis and you had a achievement for becoming a Get.<br /> <br /> (The Get &quot;bad guys&quot; in the game turn out to have been Polish partisans and they were stopped--by a Get of Fenris warrior)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:23:54-07:00","id":1484791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484759#post1484759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satire does, however, need to be updated and revised over time to maintain relevance. People only read <i>A Modest Proposal</i> to study the art of satire, not because it's actually that great of a story for 2022. Now, that doesn't mean V5 did this update well, but it not being beholden to past iterations is essential to the satire elements of the game. Basically, satire alone isn't a defense of how things were, and thus how things should be.<br /> <br /> To try to keep this thread focused on VtM at least, the loss of playable Sabbat and making Oblivion needlessly punishing to play, isn't inherently good or bad. It needs to be analyzed in how it serves the satirical commentary of contemporary society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the racism, old school VTM/V20 better reflected 2022 than V5 does. V5 reflects 2016 really well, but isn't so broadly applicable. V20 and it's first few supplements will probably remain applicable to the world for at least the next 50 years, assuming we don't blow ourselves up. It's really difficult to just undersell how timelessly great metaplot-free VTM is at satirizing modernity. WTA would've done great too were you to strip it of some tone-deaf racism and just have Pentex evolve to match concurrent trends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:24:37-07:00","id":1484792,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra have a Video game? What's it called?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:36:32-07:00","id":1484793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484789#post1484789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would I criticize what I consider a great idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just think it through for a moment. It's not a problem for you to praise idea A and Developer X, but it becomes a problem for others to criticise idea A because you've now tied it to Developer X and any heavy criticism of idea A now becomes a criticism of developer X. You, a mod, should know all to well that this can get people banned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:49:49-07:00","id":1484795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484790#post1484790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few points:<br /> <br /> 1. The Tremere only lost their<b> leadership, their blood bonds, their brand, their near-monopoly, and any semblance that they were once mostly experts who knew how to work in a large organization</b>. <br /> <br /> 2. The Hellenistic Brujah were established in the same book as them getting kicked out of the Camarilla. <b>Cool. Remember the Lasombra antitribu? What was wrong with them exactly? Why were Lasombra antis something that needed to be built upon but you're totally fine reducing the Brujah to equal or lesser level among the Camarilla? </b><br /> <br /> 3. The Lasombra have their own video game, <b>text adventure games are big, right?</b> <br /> <br /> 4. We don't know what the situation with the Get is until the book comes out. <b>Yes, V5 changed massively after the previews, right? Wrong</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh-huh. Why don't you tell us all about your love for Sabbat/Tremere while you're at it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:03:45-07:00","id":1484798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484791#post1484791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the racism,...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a pretty damned big &quot;beside.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...old school VTM/V20 better reflected 2022 than V5 does. </div> </div> </div>I agree. But that doesn't mean I agree that pre-V5 VtM is fine-as-is. VtM needed an update to the current era. V5 not being the update I wanted doesn't mean V20 is actually still a good commentary on the current state of the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:52:08-07:00","id":1484803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484795#post1484795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh-huh. Why don't you tell us all about your love for Sabbat/Tremere while you're at it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Sabbat absolutely got screwed and that they should have a playable option.<br /> <br /> *rimshot*<br /> <br /> Seriously, this is Vampire: The Masquerade not My Little Pony. I totally disagree with the idea that ANYTHING should be off limits for play if the group is comfortable with it and OPP has a much better idea of how to be &quot;adult.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484792#post1484792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra have a Video game? What's it called?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadows of New York. You play a bisexual Lasombra Neonate ex-reporter.<br /> <br /> It even incorporates Oblivion because you are brought into a murder investigation by the victim's ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-23-2022, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T15:53:09-07:00","id":1484810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484792#post1484792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra have a Video game? What's it called?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadows of new York, its a 6/10 sort of game. Visual novel style. It's about around 5 quid on steam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:40:40-07:00","id":1484821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484789#post1484789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would I criticize what I consider a great idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bringing the Lasombra to the Cam? An ok idea, I guess. The execution of it, not so much.<br /> <br /> I don't think namedropping is bad when it is to identify an actual quote, and depending on context it is relevant information. What we have to be careful about is what we say <b><i>when</i></b> namedropping. We can say anything about &quot;<i>Them</i>&quot;, because <i>They</i> are the collective result of a company where many people make many decisions and coordinating everything is hard, so no mistake necessarily means any particular person deserves the adjectives being used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484790#post1484790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few points:</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't have the same amount of vitriol about them and unneeded sarcasm as MWIS, I do have to comment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484790#post1484790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>The Council breaking apart and the clan dividing into Houses was good. Straightforward bombing the Circle and throwing the clan in complete disarray in the process, not so much. The desired effect could be achieved without crippling the clan so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484790#post1484790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The Hellenistic Brujah</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not matter, it is the whole Brujah debacle that makes no sense. I don't even thought that the Gangrel debacle made sense at its time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484790#post1484790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Lasombra have their own video game and a massively much-larger portion of the fanbase than they did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so sure about the later because they've ever been a hugely popular clan, but it makes no difference. What's being questioned is the decision of crippling them, not how popular they still came out to be regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484790#post1484790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. We don't know what the situation with the Get is until the book comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, although being wary is warranted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484803#post1484803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, this is Vampire: The Masquerade not My Little Pony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering some of the shit they did in <i>Friendship Is Magic</i>, I dare to say that <i>My Little Pony</i> would be fine with you playing the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:46:27-07:00","id":1484822,"title":"","content":"I struggle to really call it a &quot;Lasombra&quot; game. It's a VtM game with a Lasombra as the playable character. I'm wouldn't say it really relies her Clan much. I'm not sure you could have any Clan and have it make sense, but it wouldn't be hard to make the game work for most of them. You can play her as a fairly stereotypical Lasombra (or Ventrue, or Dominate focused Tremere, etc. shrewd politician) and get an ending that fits... or not and get an ending that doesn't really get the reaction from her fellow Lasombra that would make it feel more like her Clan is a major factor in the outcomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T18:13:32-07:00","id":1484831,"title":"","content":"Personally I never really saw much point in the defection, the proposed reason was redundant because their were already lasombra present within the other sect, the defection itself was badly written and made them incompetent. I'm also not particularly convinced it's done anything to affect their popularity one way or another shadows of new York is a pretty forgettable game and as heavy arms said the game isn't a particulary uniquely lasombra experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T21:09:18-07:00","id":1484839,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned my own perspective that I don't think the Lasombra were incompetent because they got accepted for doing what they would do anyway.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra had to kill all the Lasombra in the Sabbat on the way out so they didn't have their Clan seeking revenge and they even negotiated it so a &quot;Sabbat&quot; elder for every Lasombra defection.<br /> <br /> They played Kevin Jackson like a fiddle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T23:28:36-07:00","id":1484846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484821#post1484821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering some of the shit they did in <i>Friendship Is Magic</i>, I dare to say that <i>My Little Pony</i> would be fine with you playing the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I have flashbacks. How did they get that crap past S&amp;P?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T23:38:36-07:00","id":1484847,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue with the Lasombra defection iswith the Camarilla agreeing to it. Suddenly Chicago's Camarilla has brought hundreds of potential spies, saboteurs, and sleeper agents into the sect. If it were a few traitors you could keep an eye on them but this is so many its impossible. Just have cross your fingers and hope they don't destroy the sect.<br /> <br /> No matter how much I cross my eyes, I just can't see paranoid Elders agreeing to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T00:12:33-07:00","id":1484848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484847#post1484847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue with the Lasombra defection</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest issue with the Lasombra defection is that I can't see any part of this negotiation making any smart move. It is stupid to demand a suicidal genocide, it is stupid to try. The need for it was zero and the chance of success was nil, it only worked through <i>Deus-Ex-Machina</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm completely on board with the idea that you have two sides at the table that really need to make this negotiation work because of their respective circumstances, but need to keep a tight leash on each other. This is interesting and can justify a lot of risk being taken. But one side making a completely ludicrous demand because they're <b>that</b> evil, and the other accepting because they're <b>that</b> bad-ass, it just doesn't make any sense, not if taken seriously. Maybe it could fly in Warhammer 40K, because it's dark comedy.<br /> <br /> But this had been discussed at length elsewhere, the most I can say about it that is relevant to the thread is this: now the Lasombra in the Sabbat have an even greater advantage, because they don't risk losing Humanity by using their own clan Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T02:17:36-07:00","id":1484852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484848#post1484848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue with the Lasombra defection is that I can't see any part of this negotiation making any smart move. It is stupid to demand a suicidal genocide, it is stupid to try. The need for it was zero and the chance of success was nil, it only worked through <i>Deus-Ex-Machina</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm completely on board with the idea that you have two sides at the table that really need to make this negotiation work because of their respective circumstances, but need to keep a tight leash on each other. This is interesting and can justify a lot of risk being taken. But one side making a completely ludicrous demand because they're <b>that</b> evil, and the other accepting because they're <b>that</b> bad-ass, it just doesn't make <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got the impression it was Kevin Jacksons 'terms' was effectively him saying &quot;you're not joining the carmarilla.&quot; in the same sense as my demand for 5 million for my 1st print John dies at the end wasn't a serious proposal at a purchase query and then it's presented as the lasombra turned it around by agreeing as a gotcha. <br /> <br /> It could be interpreted as an accidental slam dunk for the carmarilla/ventrue that they got their primary leadership/sect rival to decapitate itself to let some bootlickers across the lines depending on if you think the ivory tower actually needs the lasombra or not. But you're completely right that it's an unmitigated disaster for the lasombra regardless of the writters trying to present it as brilliant 4d chess.<br /> <br /> But as you said-bad writting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-24-2022, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T04:58:17-07:00","id":1484858,"title":"","content":"OK to stick to Oblivion....<br /> <br /> If we're going to rehash any of the defection talk, lets focus on the fact that Oblivion as written makes the deal make even less sense. The Camarilla expects its members to upkeep their Humanity to some degree, so the Lasombra defecting to them doesn't really work well if their signature Discipline makes Humanity even harder to cope with than normal. Defecting to the Anarchs (who are closer to the Sabbat's philosophy anyway) where they would be freer to form cults that help alleviate the strain of Oblivion works a lot better.<br /> <br /> Oblivion's extra Stains ultimately make the Lasombra a harder fit for the Sect, and a better fit for the V5 take on Anarchs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T05:34:28-07:00","id":1484860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484858#post1484858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK to stick to Oblivion....<br /> <br /> If we're going to rehash any of the defection talk, lets focus on the fact that Oblivion as written makes the deal make even less sense. The Camarilla expects its members to upkeep their Humanity to some degree, so the Lasombra defecting to them doesn't really work well if their signature Discipline makes Humanity even harder to cope with than normal. Defecting to the Anarchs (who are closer to the Sabbat's philosophy anyway) where they would be freer to form cults that help alleviate the strain of Oblivion works a lot better.<br /> <br /> Oblivion's extra Stains ultimately make the Lasombra a harder fit for the Sect, and a better fit for the V5 take on Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a potential hidden benifit that if youre a ventrue/tremere since it helps re enforce the image of lasombra as erratic and unreliable. Decetivising any possibility of an challenge to ventrue leadership or tremere occult authority even further and keep them under thumb. Theirs also the nice bonus that they might just wassail so you might not have to particulary honour their refugee status for very long.<br /> <br /> The anarchs probably would have been a better option with Oblivion in mind since it would provide the sect a substantial boost to Occult power. Something they're desperately short on vs the carmarilla in v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-24-2022, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T06:39:41-07:00","id":1484864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484860#post1484860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The anarchs probably would have been a better option with Oblivion in mind since it would provide the sect a substantial boost to Occult power. Something they're desperately short on vs the carmarilla in v5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs did get the Followers of Set/Ministry, which has always been one of the more mystically aligned clans (even to the point of having a bloodline with blood magic as an in-clan discipline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T07:12:32-07:00","id":1484866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484864#post1484864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Anarchs did get the Followers of Set/Ministry, which has always been one of the more mystically aligned clans (even to the point of having a bloodline with blood magic as an in-clan discipline).</div> </div> </div> </div> Sort off but as presented in v5 that hasn't really been explored simular to any potential tzmisce kolduns. I suppose you say thin blood alchemy counts but I'd consider that bringing a knife to a sword fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T07:27:51-07:00","id":1484868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484839#post1484839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've mentioned my own perspective that I don't think the Lasombra were incompetent because they got accepted for doing what they would do anyway.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra had to kill all the Lasombra in the Sabbat on the way out so they didn't have their Clan seeking revenge and they even negotiated it so a &quot;Sabbat&quot; elder for every Lasombra defection.<br /> <br /> They played Kevin Jackson like a fiddle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book itself did not take your perspective as far as the Lasombra themselves acknowledging they had made an in some ways desperate choice in extreme circumstances that they had and will suffer for, just believing the suffering would eventually dissipate. This was noted the last time this idea was discussed and you attempted to put forward the concept that the Lasombra had managed to play the Camarilla for fools. Book got directly cited to demonstrate things like &quot;only Sabbat elders&quot; was specifically not true in other domains as far as Lasombra noting the outright harsh conditions other princes required, domains the Lasombra were noting they wanted to get into. The Amici's own perspective is &quot;a bunch of the clan that we don't want to die are going to die, but eventually the Camarilla will get tired of that.&quot; It's even simply demonstrated by Talley ending up blood hunted by his own clan as a price of the deal, despite he himself having been the one to facilitate the deal actually getting in motion and going so far as to be out there killing Cardinals to make it go, and despite being pretty much the best operative the Amici had left.<br /> <br /> There is, it feels like, a line between the V5 you want to exist, and the V5 that exists, and it sometimes blurs. This is also again one of those excluded middle things where to defend against the idea that the Lasombra perhaps didn't get the unalloyed good end of a deal, you insist that no, in fact, it was an act of ultra brilliant competence, as opposed to a bad situation they managed to handle well enough in some ways, and, being generous, with great and painful difficulty in others.<br /> <br /> They paid for their decision, they paid in ways they did not want to, and they themselves said that in their own words, in the book. As though, at bare minimum, there was an effort to not have either faction involved come off as chumps. The best you can possibly say here is that they *maybe* put one over, on some princes, and some other princes went &quot;naaaah, nice try, you bleed&quot;, and the Lasombra didn't end up with room to move around that much, and we already see someone pay for that (Talley) as an opening signifier of how not cleanly this is going to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  grammar 06-24-2022, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T13:39:11-07:00","id":1484890,"title":"","content":"Edit: Had avoided reading some parts of the Sacrifice to avoid spoilers, in case I played it, disregard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":". 06-24-2022, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T14:17:15-07:00","id":1484892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484860#post1484860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a potential hidden benifit that if youre a ventrue/tremere since it helps re enforce the image of lasombra as erratic and unreliable. Decetivising any possibility of an challenge to ventrue leadership or tremere occult authority even further and keep them under thumb. Theirs also the nice bonus that they might just wassail so you might not have to particulary honour their refugee status for very long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why it diminishes the value of the deal as a narrative element. Suiting the Ventrue and Tremere just fine without the Lasombra negotiating for anything more in return is all the more reason for the Lasombra to have flipped the deal a bird and gone elsewhere.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> As for the mysticism angle regarding the Anarchs, the Tzimisce bringing their former Sabbat allies into the Anarchs would actually help make the Anarchs a much bigger fish to contend with the Camarilla. As the Hecata have remained independent, and the Anarchs and Camarilla have both grown in their access to Blood Sorcery, only the Anarchs have prominent Oblivion users would be a tool they have and the Camarilla can only counter by outsourcing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T16:07:28-07:00","id":1484903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484847#post1484847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue with the Lasombra defection iswith the Camarilla agreeing to it. Suddenly Chicago's Camarilla has brought hundreds of potential spies, saboteurs, and sleeper agents into the sect. If it were a few traitors you could keep an eye on them but this is so many its impossible. Just have cross your fingers and hope they don't destroy the sect.<br /> <br /> No matter how much I cross my eyes, I just can't see paranoid Elders agreeing to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's why the Camarilla has them kill a Sabbat on the way out.<br /> <br /> To burn their past bridges and cripple the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla wins, the Lasombra wins.<br /> <br /> They also get the Lasombra's wealth and power when they need it most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T16:42:16-07:00","id":1484906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484903#post1484903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, that's why the Camarilla has them kill a Sabbat on the way out.<br /> <br /> To burn their past bridges and cripple the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla wins, the Lasombra wins.<br /> <br /> They also get the Lasombra's wealth and power when they need it most.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To again note, the Lasombra have been required just fine to go after non Sabbat members as part of joining the Camarilla, due, amongst other things, to various princes preferring far harsher terms to get into their cities. They've also been subject to a variety of other punitive requirements in several domains. That's right from the book. Talley was helping the Lasombra defectors kill Sabbat Lasombra and ended up on the to die list anyway, right from the book.<br /> <br /> The book tells us that the Lasombra entrance to the Camarilla will become on entirely varied terms from city to city, and that some princes are enforcing terms far more strictly, in those words, terms we get a sampling of. We read Talley himself getting effed over, and we read a Lasombra list an example of harsher terms several other domains have listed in order for their clan to get in as samples of &quot;this came at a cost.&quot;<br /> <br /> This was not some flawless master move, and treating it as one does not meaningfully intersect with the way the book writes the context of this up. The Lasombra defectors got into a real bad situation as a result of the Gehenna Crusade and the overall degeneration of the Sabbat. They made the choice to get the hell out of the Sabbat in response. They decided the best way to salvage this problem was to join the Camarilla. They handled that as skillfully as they could manage in the circumstances. It was not without its price, they acknowledged of themselves it would have a price, and not one &quot;that they were doing anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to debate whether or not the writing was effective/resonant in conveying the idea that the Lasombra joined the Camarilla in a way that both benefitted and costed them in meaningful ways, or that said joining otherwise made sense as a choice based on its provided details. It's another to insist &quot;the Lasombra were killing the Sabbat Lasombra anyway and they only had to kill Sabbat Lasombra, joining the Camarilla was a masterstroke that impaired them in no way and not one they paid any real price for doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is how this keeps reading. If that's not actually what is meant here, hey sure, parsing text online can be a thing, but if it is, these claims are going one way, and the book content is going a different way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-24-2022, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T03:59:56-07:00","id":1484957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484892#post1484892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's why it diminishes the value of the deal as a narrative element. Suiting the Ventrue and Tremere just fine without the Lasombra negotiating for anything more in return is all the more reason for the Lasombra to have flipped the deal a bird and gone elsewhere.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> As for the mysticism angle regarding the Anarchs, the Tzimisce bringing their former Sabbat allies into the Anarchs would actually help make the Anarchs a much bigger fish to contend with the Camarilla. As the Hecata have remained independent, and the Anarchs and Camarilla have both grown in their access to Blood Sorcery, only the Anarchs have prominent Oblivion users would be a tool they have and the Camarilla can only counter by outsourcing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yeah it doesn't help that it's noted the lasombra don't even really bother with the rituals genrally so they're not even the best at death magic.<br /> <br /> As presented in previous edition the clans obtenerbration combined with potence is outright brutal in combat so they could when combined with the assamites they could have &quot;it'll do&quot; filled the gangrel/brujah hole with revised/v20 rules. This could work if they didn't have the issue with marks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-25-2022, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T08:17:59-07:00","id":1484966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484903#post1484903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also get the Lasombra's wealth and power when they need it most.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't &quot;need it most&quot; if they hadn't have scooped out their fucking brains and bullshitted half the sect and the Brujah out. You should also consider Lasombra wealth absolutely devastated by their Sabbat rebellion. This isn't three steps forward and two steps back, it's nine steps back and one sideways. Your wilful ignorance is painful to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T14:37:10-07:00","id":1484987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484966#post1484966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wouldn't &quot;need it most&quot; if they hadn't have scooped out their fucking brains and bullshitted half the sect and the Brujah out. You should also consider Lasombra wealth absolutely devastated by their Sabbat rebellion. This isn't three steps forward and two steps back, it's nine steps back and one sideways. Your wilful ignorance is painful to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the rich Brujah stayed with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> All the Camarilla lost was a Justicar, an Inner Councilman (who was assassinated anyway according to THE CAMARILLA), and the need to protect the Neonates of the most rebellious clan.<br /> <br /> And the Lasombra didn't lose a dime. The Sabbat as they stand aren't going to be able to wage economic warfare on the Lasombra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T14:54:38-07:00","id":1484991,"title":"","content":"So, my issue with Oblivion is twofold: Perverse Incentives and Opportunity Cost.<br /> <br /> The Perverse Incentives has been well established in this thread. When you create a Discipline whose downsides are so severe, you encourage players to never use it. Or to use it so sparingly as to call into question why you bothered to invest in it or the Clan in the first place. (More on that when I discuss Opportunity Cost).<br /> <br /> A game mechanic ought to, by its design, encourage players to do what you want them to do.<br /> <br /> Example: the Ventrue have a combination of Disciplines and Weakness that funnels them towards acquiring influence and accumulating Herd, and makes them very good at it. Which is what Ventrue are intended to be about. Their unique combination of game mechanics organically reinforces the Clan narrative. Even if you had a Ventrue fledgling entirely divorced from their Clan upon Embrace, for whatever reason, they would naturally trend towards the same general unlifestyle, albeit without all the pretensions of nobility or corporate atmosphere. The patterns of manipulating people and bringing vessels into one's orbit arises naturally from their particular strengths and needs.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean a Ventrue is enslaved to this paradigm. Merely that they're swimming against the tide, while moving with it is much easier and more lucrative.<br /> <br /> Oblivion makes it hazardous to be any kind of Humane vampire. This wouldn't be as bad if V5 made adopting a Path possible. But as established, V5 seems from executive fiat to be hostile to Paths as a concept. Nor, as we've seen, can Tenets/Convictions cover for it, RAW. We can house rule it, but that cedes the central point: V5, as written, is not fit for purpose.<br /> <br /> It's not even that the game <i>needed</i> to give Lasombra Stains for using their signature Discipline. Doing the kinds of things Obtenebration/Oblivion is good at naturally puts one in situations where degenerating is likely. They didn't really need to make it uniquely evil and soul-crushing. They chose to, because they made an authorial value judgement about Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Combined with the lack of Paths and the general hostility to letting people play Sabbat, and it gives the definite impression that the designers did not want anyone playing Lasombra.<br /> <br /> If this wasn't their intention, they have a funny way of showing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the subject of Opportunity Cost, by taking a Clan whose signature Discipline gives you Stains from using it, you're being punished by the game design for not playing a different one. Other Disciplines don't have a chance to give you Stains just from use. You're encouraged to either not invest your Lasombra's XP into Oblivion - running against the primary draw of the Clan - or not to take Lasombra at all.<br /> <br /> Not only is this bad game design, it's unfair to people who wanted to play Lasombra. Fans of the Clan not only have them ripped out of the Sabbat where they were accustomed, they're told in a roundabout way that their favorite Clan is Bad Wrong Fun.<br /> <br /> Nor should a gaming group need to disregard published material, the most current and supported version of Vampire: The Masquerade, just to play their favorite Clan the way they always could in the past. All for the sake of a game mechanic that didn't need to work that way in the first place, and doesn't meaningfully make V5 better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T15:07:28-07:00","id":1484994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484987#post1484987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Lasombra didn't lose a dime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give a page reference for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-25-2022, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T20:48:48-07:00","id":1485007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484987#post1484987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the rich Brujah stayed with the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a reference?<br /> <br /> Why would they if the Cam jetisoned the rest of the clan? Wouldn't that lack of a base weaken then anyway?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484987#post1484987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Camarilla lost was a Justicar, an Inner Councilman (who was assassinated anyway according to THE CAMARILLA), and the need to protect the Neonates of the most rebellious clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the &quot;rich Brujah&quot; stay in the sect after being stripped of the two positions that were meant for the &quot;rich Brujah&quot;? And why would they stop protecting Neonates of any clan if their MO is to offer protection to Neonates to placate them against the elders?<br /> <br /> This makes no sense whatsoever, and AFAIK stems only from your own personal canon, not from any official source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1484987#post1484987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Lasombra didn't lose a dime. The Sabbat as they stand aren't going to be able to wage economic warfare on the Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that a short genocidal civil war against equally capable Lasombra, followed by fleeing your home and leaving everything behind, somehow had zero net cost or even resulted in profit is naive to a degree I won't put into words out of respect.<br /> <br /> Defectors are basically refugees. They can bring something with them to their new homes, and sometimes some of them are able to get richer, but the vast majority will cross the line leaving most of their assets behind, because really transferring all those is far more complicated on most situations, and there's no reason to believe this was an exception.<br /> <br /> Vampires do not have their assets mostly in the form of Bank Accounts, neither do they somehow learn from their dead enemies things like bank accounts and passwords, unless you're working with really weird Diablerie rules. They would barely be able to carry most of their personal effects with them. Most assets are intrinsically tied to things that remain in your city unless you take great pains to move them or keep in contact. Seizing the belongings left behind by defectors is standard practice.<br /> <br /> How on Earth do you think the Lasombra defectors managed to whisk away everything they possessed plus spoils without any significant cost? Please, if you don't have an actual reference at least present an explanation for the logistics of this prodigious plan.<br /> <br /> If you can't either provide an actual reference or a sensible plan, then please stop stating it as a fact instead of as your chronicle's canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T22:54:57-07:00","id":1485015,"title":"","content":"Since the issue of &quot;where are you even getting this from&quot; is becoming a central thing: Just so no one feels I said &quot;this is directly from the book&quot; without offering up something more concrete, you can find the concept that the Lasombra in fact had to make meaningful sacrifices, endure meaningfully bad treatment, will have to deal with harsher policies than Kevin Jackson's, that their entry to the Camarilla is an uneven one that, in some of the following places of Chicago By Night for 5th edition Vampire. They establish that even in a forgiving read, the entry to the Camarilla had ups and downs for the Lasombra, that the downs are not something you can just &quot;meh&quot; away.<br /> <br /> On page 40 of the book, a member of the Lasombra clan describes the harsh strictures at least several cities are already laying out as the price of the Clan's entry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The weak cities, the ones who lost half their<br /> Kindred population to the Anarchs, they\u2019re the ones<br /> saying we just need to deliver the staked bodies of Sabbat<br /> troublemakers, Lasombra or not. The conservative<br /> domains? The ones we want to get in on? They\u2019ve been<br /> known to ask for the following:<br /> \u2022 For every Lasombra joining the Camarilla, an elder<br /> Lasombra must be presented as sacrifice.<br /> \u2022 Lasombra intending on joining the Camarilla must<br /> submit to a Blood Bond.<br /> \u2022 A maximum of three Lasombra may exist in any<br /> one Camarilla domain.<br /> \u2022 Lasombra are to receive no warnings regarding the<br /> Traditions; just punishment.<br /> \u2022 The practice of our particular brand of blood arts is<br /> forbidden on pain of final death.<br /> \u2022 No Lasombra may hold title in Camarilla domains<br /> for at least 50 years.<br /> I could go on. The Camarilla love this new power<br /> they have over us. </div> </div> </div>While Talley getting the ol eff over despite his services, in part because the Camarilla want important lasombra to die, Sabbat or no Sabbat, is noted in several places in the book, my personal favorite is on page 292, as it highlights that coming down, even as he just finishes taking out a Sabbat Cardinal for the defectors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sudden blast of heat from the gasoline-steeped<br /> Cardinal Renate made Talley step back, shielding his eyes.<br /> A very mortal gesture. Talley corrected himself to watch the<br /> body burn. Tracking Renate, seizing her, and staking her<br /> ultimately came down to which of them was better skilled in<br /> the Lasombra arts. It had been a grueling task, but not an<br /> unpleasant one.<br /> As his ghoul started typing \u201cIt is done\u201d into Talley\u2019s phone,<br /> the few lights in the alley blinked off one by one. The shadows<br /> drew in, plunging the entire area into blackness. Talley cast<br /> about, looking for the source of this sorcery. His eyes pierced the<br /> unnatural gloom, but found nothing. A sound made him turn<br /> toward the fire. The Cardinal\u2019s body was gone, nothing left but<br /> the flames dying down. A stump of the stake was resting in the<br /> ash. \u201cMaybe we\u2019ll meet again sooner than planned, my dear.\u201d<br /> Talley dusted ash from his jacket as his accomplice at<br /> the other end of the alley spoke up. \u201cBy order of the Friends of<br /> the Night, you\u2019re next to go, Sir Talley.\u201d Shadows throughout<br /> the alley rapidly converged on the Templar, snaking along the<br /> walls and across the ground while his assailant maintained<br /> their distance. Talley watched as the tendrils approached,<br /> and considered for a second before nodding respectfully at his<br /> murderous childe, and vaulted into the dark. </div> </div> </div>And then there is the sidebar in the adventure proper, noting in third person objective narration no less, the experience of the Amici Noctis themselves, the ones in charge of this whole thing, that the Camarilla will in fact kill members of their clan they don't want to die, they just assume the Camarilla will realize eventually that is counter productive once enough Lasombra die, and that in the meantime they will just carve out exceptions for themselves and some others. The sidebar goes so far as to tell us that Princes will in fact deviate just fine from Kevin Jackson's pact, and sometimes that is going to be bad for the Lasombra. &quot;Tire of the taste of Lasombra blood&quot;, is not the sort of writing a person can realistically claim goes with &quot;ha ha! the fools! we lost nothing!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LETTER OF THE DEAL<br /> If followed to the extreme, Clan Lasombra could<br /> find its numbers radically reduced as a result of<br /> Prince Jackson\u2019s pact, though so far it only extends<br /> to Lasombra seeking domain in Chicago.<br /> It\u2019s an appealing deal to many Camarilla Princes<br /> however, so depending on its success, other<br /> Princes such as Decker of Milwaukee might soon<br /> adopt it.<br /> Of course, the letter of the deal was not to deliver<br /> elders of the Lasombra, but elders of the<br /> Sabbat. Princes interpret this rule differently, and<br /> before the Justicars know it, individual Princes are<br /> enforcing their own Lasombra admittance rules.<br /> Some are more relaxed than others, some are far<br /> stricter.<br /> The Amici Noctis believe the Camarilla will tire<br /> of the taste of Lasombra blood when they realize<br /> they are purging useful Keepers in the same<br /> way Stalin executed almost all his effective military<br /> officers. Until then, however, they will state<br /> which Lasombra are exempt from the internal<br /> hunt. Obviously, the Amici Noctis are on top of<br /> the exemption list. </div> </div> </div>That's from page 335. There's other things certainly, but the point is when you look at all of this together, or at least when I do, it creates a very obvious context that no, the Lasombra didn't pull off some flawless brilliant move where all they did was what they were already doing, and suffered no real consequences thusly, nor real losses, and they played everyone in their way for fools. Can it be argued that with regards some Princes, the Lasombra came out better? Sure. Can it also be argued that with regards other domains, and with an example given outright of a non Sabbat elder having to be given up along with notes that others will suffer likewise (hey, at least Talley is surviving the blood hunt so far), and notes of punitive conditions, that they did not come out all that well at all? The book looks strongly like it supports doing so. As though the situation overall, is mixed. To say something like &quot;the Lasombra killed only the Sabbat they wanted to kill&quot; when the book talks about the Amici having to deal with the Camarilla &quot;purging useful Keepers&quot; in those exact words, is somewhat baffling and would require ignoring all these passages and the context they create coming together, because of course, in an overall book, things don't exist in a vaccuum. They create context. That's just how writing works.<br /> <br /> Whether someone thinks it was successfully written or not (and from several threads now, a number of posters here just don't find it to have been convincingly put together), the book clearly at least <b>tried</b> to offer a portrayal of the Lasombra defection and joining of the Camarilla as one containing both ups and downs for the Lasombra defectors/the clan as a whole. To continue to insist on an extreme reading of that material regardless as some masterpiece political move without cost, it just doesn't work with the actual book. If there was some intent to instead say something like the writing becomes contradictory on itself for how the deal was good or bad or not, even that would be more substantial than what is being put forward as it stands.<br /> <br /> Again, there is a substantial difference between someone trying to say that they don't find a particular plot development to have been well or convincingly written, and note various plot holes, logic gaps, things that make no sense to them, or to instead for some reason say the equivalent of that actual content of the book that exists, does not exist. It would be one thing to reply with opinions of why instead the writing does feel convincing, hangs together, etc, maybe give some examples, so forth. It's something else for someone to just seemingly decide anything that disagrees with their stance was not written or, for whatever reason, completely ignore stuff right from the book regardless when making claims about plot, book content, etc..<br /> <br /> If that's not the intent here, certainly my bad. But it's at the very least hard to parse anything else out of the discourse at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  I used the word certainly something like eleventy million times in this post. Also other minor touch ups. 06-26-2022, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T00:19:10-07:00","id":1485020,"title":"","content":"There's some definite V5 reasons for why the people did what they did. If you don't like V5 developments, of course they won't be that way.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Why did the Camarilla jettison the Brujah</b>: The idea is that the Camarilla no longer felt the desire to waste resources on the Brujah given that they were part of the assassination of Hardelstadt. The Camarilla is &quot;hunkering down&quot; throughout V5 and attempting to preserve the wealthy and powerful of their ranks as well as presumably the non-Beckoned Elders because it's a gerontocracy. Everyone else is getting thrown to the wolves.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>V5's metaplot is Transylvania Chronicles: The Sequel</b>: Part of what you either agree about or disagree about V5 is that the metaplor is basically Pam from True Blood saying, &quot;The worst<br /> part of immortality is seeing the same stupid ship happen over and over again.&quot; In this case, much of the metaplot is just repeating all of the Anarch Revolt from the Dark Ages happening again. The Inquisition happens, the Elders throw the Neonates to the Inquisitors, and this results in a strengthened Anarch movement.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Why did the Lasombra leave</b>: Well we have the Sabbat book out and retroactively, it's clear the Lasombra saw the writing on the wall. The Sabbat became a bunch of degenerate horde monsters and animals, so of course teh Lasombra are going to avoid becoming a horde of locusts.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>How good is the Lasombra deal?</b>: I feel like the interpretation is that yes the Lasombra had to make sacrifices but I point out the Lasombra didn't have to leave behind their cities and wealth because <i>the Sabbat already did that</i>. V5's Sabbat are not keepers of territory and don't keep their wealth. I feel like they made the best choice they could have under the circumstances.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>How powerful will the Lasombra be?</b>: The Camarilla is lacking a large chunk of its Elders, has lost two Clans, has lost many more of its members to the Second Inquisition, and also suffered some truly humiliating defeats (Vienna Chantry, Hardelstadt). The Lasombra are perfect for moving in, alongside the Banu Haqim, and making a lot bigger place for themselves in the Ivory Tower than might have normally been possible.<br /> <br /> There was never a better time for defection but it's not like they had a choice if the Black Hand book is correct because the Sabbat drank ALL the kool aid.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was not perfect perhaps but the best decision they could make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T00:32:04-07:00","id":1485021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but I point out the Lasombra didn't have to leave behind their cities</div> </div> </div> </div>Page reference? Because there are actual printed words saying the Lasombra are trying to get into cities where they did not have a real presence before (some of them quoted even in this thread). That literally, and this verges on being a rare case where the word literally is possibly being used correctly, means any number of them had to leave cities, to go to other cities, and try to be acknowledged in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. <b>How powerful will the Lasombra be?</b>: The Camarilla is lacking a large chunk of its Elders, has lost two Clans, has lost many more of its members to the Second Inquisition, and also suffered some truly humiliating defeats (Vienna Chantry, Hardelstadt). The Lasombra are perfect for moving in, alongside the Banu Haqim, and making a lot bigger place for themselves in the Ivory Tower than might have normally been possible. </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra are down a significant chunk of their clan, and are suffering their own Elder losses. Times aren't great for them either. <br /> <br /> I mean the game wants them to be a playable clan, and the Sabbat are no longer playable, so something will work out I'm sure, but where things currently stand, neither they, nor the Camarilla as a sect, are doing all that well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T01:59:08-07:00","id":1485025,"title":"","content":"The odd thing is the defection is completly redundant their where already lasombra in the carmarilla not to mention the possibility of ashira refugees ala the assamites. <br /> The presence of tzmisce anarchs was far better written on reflection.<br /> <br /> But back on subject how many people just flat out ignored the rule? I know I did.<br /> <br /> I've noticed a similar rule in previous editions where a Thaumaturgy botch caused the loss of a willpower point, I think this becomes more acceptable due to low risk/high reward ratio in the discipline. Could the issue of humanity loss be countered by boosting the raw power of necromancy/obtenerbration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-26-2022, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T02:25:34-07:00","id":1485026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some definite V5 reasons for why the people did what they did. If you don't like V5 developments, of course they won't be that way.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Why did the Camarilla jettison the Brujah</b>: The idea is that the Camarilla no longer felt the desire to waste resources on the Brujah given that they were part of the assassination of Hardelstadt. The Camarilla is &quot;hunkering down&quot; throughout V5 and attempting to preserve the wealthy and powerful of their ranks as well as presumably the non-Beckoned Elders because it's a gerontocracy. Everyone else is getting thrown to the wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>-The Brujah offer a massive amount of resources and it costs a massive amount of resources to go against the Brujah. <br /> -Nobody (in universe) gives a fuck about Theo Bell and hardestardt the whatever. They don't bother the overwhewlming majority of princes, so making a big deal out of this is rediculous. <br /> (also It's not a very convincing assassination for a long list of reasons but that's besides the point) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. <b>V5's metaplot is Transylvania Chronicles: The Sequel</b>: Part of what you either agree about or disagree about V5 is that the metaplor is basically Pam from True Blood saying, &quot;The worst<br /> part of immortality is seeing the same stupid ship happen over and over again.&quot; In this case, much of the metaplot is just repeating all of the Anarch Revolt from the Dark Ages happening again. The Inquisition happens, the Elders throw the Neonates to the Inquisitors, and this results in a strengthened Anarch movement. </div> </div> </div>Except the political and historical context that allowed the FI is not at all present for the SI. Next big anarch revolt? Sure, but not another large scale vampire hunt. It goes against today's zietgiest to boot. . <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. <b>Why did the Lasombra leave</b>: Well we have the Sabbat book out and retroactively, it's clear the Lasombra saw the writing on the wall. The Sabbat became a bunch of degenerate horde monsters and animals, so of course teh Lasombra are going to avoid becoming a horde of locusts.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>How good is the Lasombra deal?</b>: I feel like the interpretation is that yes the Lasombra had to make sacrifices but I point out the Lasombra didn't have to leave behind their cities and wealth because <i>the Sabbat already did that</i>. V5's Sabbat are not keepers of territory and don't keep their wealth. I feel like they made the best choice they could have under the circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> 5. <b>How powerful will the Lasombra be?</b>: The Camarilla is lacking a large chunk of its Elders, has lost two Clans, has lost many more of its members to the Second Inquisition, and also suffered some truly humiliating defeats (Vienna Chantry, Hardelstadt). The Lasombra are perfect for moving in, alongside the Banu Haqim, and making a lot bigger place for themselves in the Ivory Tower than might have normally been possible.<br /> <br /> There was never a better time for defection but it's not like they had a choice if the Black Hand book is correct because the Sabbat drank ALL the kool aid.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was not perfect perhaps but the best decision they could make. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For the sake of my sanity I'm not continue beating this dead horse. </span></span></span>It'd probably be saner to start fucking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T02:41:54-07:00","id":1485027,"title":"","content":"It sounds like many of the justifications for writers screwing over the Sabbat are basically the other examples of writers screwing over the Sabbat. Which is why I've massively toned down the changes to the metaplot in my games. In my games, the Sabbat have lost several cities due to Cathari demagogues taking over and encouraging hedonistic stupidity. Which is quickly leading the sect towards civil war, with an alliance of Feral Hearters, Honorable Accordists, and Death and Sout types set to topple the Cathari demagogues and possibly even declare the Cathari path heretical. It's going to be rough, because the Cathari demagogues are especially popular amongst the very young, so the real Sabbat are going to have to plow their way through a lot of shovelhead trash who should have never been raised to true Sabbat status.<br /> <br /> Anyway the Lasombra are kind of a mess this edition. Their bane doesn't fit a High Clan, and feels more like an alternate universe bane for the Gangrel. Their signature discipline now costs Humanity and they aren't allowed to adopt a Path anymore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T02:54:53-07:00","id":1485028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485027#post1485027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway the Lasombra are kind of a mess this edition. Their bane doesn't fit a High Clan, and feels more like an alternate universe bane for the Gangrel. Their signature discipline now costs Humanity and they aren't allowed to adopt a Path anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its also worth noting the cappadocians in heceta also loose out with this in mind. Cappadocians historically where a respected high clan and often relied upon as advisors and academics. Them being more susceptible to degeneration and Wassail doesn't really mesh.<br /> <br /> It works a little better with giovanni but it's been clear that the giovanni's issues come from culture rather than nature.<br /> Although naraja shouldnt be on humanity full stop.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also your Sabbat plot is fucking amazing-youve spun gold from shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-26-2022, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T07:52:01-07:00","id":1485031,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna try to help CTPhipps out for a minute here.<br /> <br /> To be fair, some Lasombra did in fact manage to hold onto such power as they clawed out for themselves in places, right from the book. For example, there's a bit from a member of the clan about how the Clan still holds onto their Church influence, apparently in the face of retaining little all else, to the point of looking like they have no other mortal influence coming into new cities. Though it's honestly... not that impressive for the shine they try to put on how important it is that they did when they have to talk about it in the terms of 'it may look like we lost all our influence, but we have this one very specific thing still!'. Even a description of a specifically influential Lasombra is counterbalanced by a gripe that they lost all the ways they used to ply influence more unsubtly when they left the Sabbat, but we'll talk about that in a minute. Because also, from the book, others did not hold onto such things. With, for instance, Talley noting that some Lasombra will be taking the Camarilla's money to work as their enforcers. This is not a thing wealthy people need to do. Otherwise, as far as some Lasombra having had to indeed leave their previous place behind, when the word &quot;migration&quot; gets used, the notion that they pretty all much kicked back in place, chilln out, maxin' relaxin' all cool while shooting some b ball outside of the school, does not bear out. The part where by contrast some of them got in one little fight and their mom got scared and said &quot;you're moving with your Auntie and Uncle in Bel Air&quot;, does. Even simply from that the initial clusters of envoys had to go to various Camarilla cities to ask to be let in, let alone stuff about wanting to be entire presences in cities where the clan has not been.<br /> <br /> So again, like everything else, it's a mixed portrayal, or it's at least an effort thereby at a mixed portrayal, further underscored in this case that you are dealing with Lasombra talking about Lasombra, meaning that even while there's a grain of salt qualifier for their statements, that applies to both when they talk about how things are still good, and how bad things have got. Likely again the book trying to go &quot;the truth lies somewhere in the middle.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem people are having is not that it reads like they especially disagree that the book tried to say all this kind of thing. The problem they are having is that they feel the book said all this kind of thing *badly*, in a way that does not, for them, sufficiently paper over the logic holes, plot gaps, and the like, something like this entire sequence would expose, even just from writing trying to say the defection had both positive and negative aspects. That it all just feels like a mess.<br /> <br /> &quot;The book can say what it says, but here is why that thing it said would make no sense/feel entirely inconsistent if you think about it.&quot;, or &quot;the book can say this thing, but they did not say it in a convincing way for not actually addressing the issues incident x should cause&quot; is the heart of the note, with various elaborations.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it is worth talking about the whole Doylist vs Watsonian textual approach thing, because this thread is definitely crashing into it. People are saying stuff that boils down to not buying into the underlying narrative craft for feeling the writing choices gloss over whole huge issues that logically should have been problems. Or, to try for half a second to be topical to the thread topic, when they say the actual implications of the punitive game mechanics of the Lasombra's own discipline themselves are an obstacle to what the in setting justifications of the defection want to be, in many ways it isn't satisfying to reply to either of these issues &quot;well, as long as you see that it is justifiable within setting..&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem here is that this is a development meant to serve a meta narrative reason: The Sabbat are not playable in this edition, but the developers want the Lasombra be. So they did a plot to try and salvage that. The choices made for how to write that plot are, certainly for the people posting in this thread, ones that instead of smoothing the meta decision over, raise entirely new gripes of narrative cohesion and consistency with just a bunch of previous plot, or even more basic concepts of logic like &quot;that it didn't screw them up even worse is not believable due to how cause and effect works, even if the writing claims it is&quot;. I can say &quot;well, within the setting's internal narrative, this is why they regardless had to do that, and these are the costs they paid&quot;, and I did, and you can say that, and you eventually got there somewhat more accurately than before, but saying that doesn't actually solve for those issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-26-2022, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T09:29:58-07:00","id":1485033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485021#post1485021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page reference? Because there are actual printed words saying the Lasombra are trying to get into cities where they did not have a real presence before (some of them quoted even in this thread). That literally, and this verges on being a rare case where the word literally is possibly being used correctly, means any number of them had to leave cities, to go to other cities, and try to be acknowledged in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire Black Hand book because the reason they don't lose their cities is the Sabbat abandoned them first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T09:30:21-07:00","id":1485034,"title":"","content":"I <i>really</i> don't think the devs intended you to play the Lasombra. In context with everything, putting the Lasombra into the Camarilla is really more a statement of &quot;Look how far the Cam has fallen, to have replaced the clan known for their strong opinions (Brujah) with the psychopathic Authoritarian-Bastard clan&quot;. In V20, you play Sabbat if you want to have fun as moustache twirling villains, in V5, If you want an &quot;evil campaign&quot; you play the flanderized nuCamarilla; the Anarchs are the intended default for protagonists. <br /> <br /> Yet, because the creators of V5 view Lasombra as &quot;wrong&quot; they've done their best to sabotage and neuter them. Where once you had a the most aggressive-bastard clan with three big hammers for disciplines and a weakness that makes them paranoid control freaks/was given to them for just being too damn despicable. A clan of sociopaths (for sociopaths): now you have a clan that needs a ghoul to babysit and take their calls for them. A clan with three of the hardest-hit disciplines in V5. A clan that accepted an unconditional surrender en-masse because they couldn't control the organization they were running. The Lasombra in V5 are a joke, and it just goes to show that the Camarilla in V5 are a joke. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T09:40:57-07:00","id":1485036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485033#post1485033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The entire Black Hand book because the reason they don't lose their cities is the Sabbat abandoned them first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That does not address that any numbers of Lasombra, once again, rare correct use, literally left the cities they were previously in to go to Camarilla cities they were not in. The Sabbat abandoning cities does not mean by default the defector Lasombra got to keep them. They are intentionally attempting to spread their numbers into existing Camarilla domains. That's part of their entire plan.<br /> <br /> On sheer simple narrative construction, if a concerted effort to move into new places is happening, it means the old places are being left by the people moving into new places.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even address the idea that considering they had to go to war with their brethren, and war involves loss and sacrifice. They are, as a mission statement, running the hell away from the Sabbat. When you are running away from a thing, you leave places where that thing is doing stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-26-2022, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T09:50:04-07:00","id":1485037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In V20, you play Sabbat if you want to have fun as moustache twirling villains, </div> </div> </div>Not for nothing, but while not the world's biggest fan of the Sabbat, there was more to do with them in V20 than play them as moustache twirling villains, and we've seen a hojillion threads at this point of fans of the Sabbat going into such things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want an &quot;evil campaign&quot; you play the flanderized nuCamarilla; the Anarchs are the intended default for protagonists. </div> </div> </div>I will however agree that &quot;playing the Camarilla is an evil choice for evil&quot; is something that characterizes V5 and a lot of work was put in to make the sect the busted up cartoon that fits that mission statement. And that there are outright &quot;the Anarchs are the protagonists now&quot; stuff, and so forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>really</i> don't think the devs intended you to play the Lasombra. </div> </div> </div>In my view, it is ultimately more constructive to discussion to not assume they were bald faced lying when they say they do want you to play them and to simply consider how successful or not they were at the idea that they kept the clan playable. You can at least squint and see what they would have been thinking. You can then note why that didn't in practice actually work out, but I think it's reasonable to believe that some kind of try was made.<br /> <br /> (That said, if you were to ask me if I honestly believed they wanted anyone to play a Salubri again, I'd have a much harder time there)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T12:55:41-07:00","id":1485046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485026#post1485026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The Brujah offer a massive amount of resources and it costs a massive amount of resources to go against the Brujah.<br /> -Nobody (in universe) gives a fuck about Theo Bell and hardestardt the whatever. They don't bother the overwhewlming majority of princes, so making a big deal out of this is rediculous.<br /> (also It's not a very convincing assassination for a long list of reasons but that's besides the point)</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, I'm asking what Brujah you think were kicked out that would benefit over staying? No, they don't have a Justicar or inner councilman but Maxwell is still a Prince (albeit of Gary), the Wolf Pack are still Archons (albeit Gangrel), and Critias is still Primogen.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Brujah lost some prestige but the Hellenistic ones are still there.<br /> <br /> Why? Because they were invested in the system.<br /> <br /> Really, they just expelled most of the ANARCHS from the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T13:35:42-07:00","id":1485048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485046#post1485046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, I'm asking what Brujah you think were kicked out that would benefit over staying? No, they don't have a Justicar or inner councilman but Maxwell is still a Prince (albeit of Gary), the Wolf Pack are still Archons (albeit Gangrel), .</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you talk about Gangrel Archons when trying to claim something about the Brujah? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, they just expelled most of the ANARCHS from the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>It is noted in the Camarilla book by Damian that enough non Anarch Brujah left the Camarilla to put a dent in various cities Primogen councils and reduce the Camarilla's boots on the ground strength in such places. The idea that but some sprinkling of Cam Brujah left does not bear out. Enough Brujah went in full to the Anarchs that were not Anarchs before that the Brujah are now considered a primary Anarch clan, as opposed to a clan where a bunch of them are Anarchs. That last part is just.. the Brujah being noted as one of the Anarch clans now, that's just sheer logistics. For that to be the case it has to mean that enough Brujah that were not anarchs before, became anarchs, to tip the scale that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T15:01:49-07:00","id":1485058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485048#post1485048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would you talk about Gangrel Archons when trying to claim something about the Brujah?</div> </div> </div> </div>As an example of how a Clan leaving doesn't affect the power base of individual vampires in the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is noted in the Camarilla book by Damian that enough non Anarch Brujah left the Camarilla to put a dent in various cities Primogen councils and reduce the Camarilla's boots on the ground strength in such places. The idea that but some sprinkling of Cam Brujah left does not bear out. Enough Brujah went in full to the Anarchs that were not Anarchs before that the Brujah are now considered a primary Anarch clan, as opposed to a clan where a bunch of them are Anarchs. That last part is just.. the Brujah being noted as one of the Anarch clans now, that's just sheer logistics. For that to be the case it has to mean that enough Brujah that were not anarchs before, became anarchs, to tip the scale that way. </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, the Brujah have always been primarily Anarchs in terms of numbers. It's just the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs part of the Camarilla.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T15:20:34-07:00","id":1485060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some definite V5 reasons for why the people did what they did. If you don't like V5 developments, of course they won't be that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this has been acknowledged and considered, but doesn't mean we have to, even then, agree either that the Doylist reasons are good, that the Watsonian justifications are sound, or that the actual execution was well done.<br /> <br /> You are consistently defending those developments based on how <b>you</b> use then on your chronicles, while people are arguing what's actually in the books. We know it isn't rocket science to adapt bad writing to make a good game, most here have more than a decade as STs under our belts, some have three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why did the Camarilla jettison the Brujah</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the Watsonian justification. I still don't think it makes sense, even if you assume the Doylist goal as worth it, which I don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>V5's metaplot is Transylvania Chronicles: The Sequel</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is an interesting thing to do with an adventure, not with the whole game. And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> said, it actually follows the trope of &quot;History Repeats Itself&quot; without grasping any of the context, how History actually works.<br /> <br /> Newsflash: History is a science that real people have a varying grasp on, you can't say whatever you want about it and expect everyone to find it believable. It's as prone to Disbelief as any other thing in a story, and the problem here is that for many people the Suspension was broken. Not for you? Good for <b>you</b>, but while the Suspension of Disbelief is a personal matter, the onus of helping or breaking it is on the author.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why did the Lasombra leave</b></div> </div> </div> </div>No one argued their reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How good is the Lasombra deal?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't previously said they had to make sacrifices. You said consistently and repeatedly that they made a genius move without any downside they wouldn't do anyway, and you said it was supported by the books, which it isn't. It is a generous interpretation of what lies beyond the books.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> said, the whole thing is about the Lasombra fleeing to Camarilla cities. The books do <u><b>not</b></u>, by any stretch, support the idea that the Lasombra rebuilt their power bases in the territory vacated by the Sabbat, they consistently state that the Lasombra are fleeing for Camarilla cities. So they <b>are </b>leaving their things behind.<br /> <br /> This is not hard to imagine, either. If the Sabbat will leave the city behind, &quot;burning the fields&quot; would be a logical action, and as crazy as they are, they still have half a brain. &quot;The Lasombra left for the Cam, lets destroy everything they had here before leaving&quot;. Not to mention that unless the Lasombra want to hold those domains on their own, which they explicitly didn't even tried, the coming Cam they allied with will take hold and probably grab a lot of the stuff the Lasombra had, even as payment. The Lasombra wouldn't be able to do much, as they would have to flee the city at least at first to avoid being hunted down by the Sabbat before it leaves.<br /> <br /> I do think, by the way, that the Cam may have used the opportunity to establish new domains under the defection by sending new Princes and enforcers to abandoned cities with local Lasombra populations, but it would be far more cautious on those places and be selling the annexation as protection, which in a sense it is. A high-risk, high-reward project for the entrepreneuring Prince. This can be used to make a number of interesting chronicles with a greater number of Lasombra in the city, probably as &quot;second-class citizens&quot; (until and <b>if</b> they usurp the power).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How powerful will the Lasombra be?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra lost as much or more than the Cam, especially because of the way the defection was played. If they had simply left the Sabbat silently, they would come with less of a hit to their human resources, specially highly skilled elders that can't be replaced in a pinch. Even skilled Ancillae and Neonates take time and effort to replace, they're not Fledglings. Instead they were required to go to war with themselves and off a lot of the same skilled resources they need.<br /> <br /> So, while it is true that this is a prime moment for the defection, which is the very reason why the Camarilla (that isn't a bunch of imbeciles, either) accepted it in bulk, it had to, they're in a terrible shape to properly seize the opportunity. And on top of that the Cam is perfectly aware and wary of this opportunity and of the Lasombra taking it, so there are several caveats to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485020#post1485020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it was not perfect perhaps but the best decision they could make.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one objects that the defection was, given the circumstances, a good option. What's being argued is that the terms of the defection are badly written and definitely not the best any of the sides could have created and agreed upon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485027#post1485027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their signature discipline now costs Humanity and they aren't allowed to adopt a Path anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it is worth for the actual thread, this is a huge problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T16:42:21-07:00","id":1485063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485058#post1485058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> From my perspective, the Brujah have always been primarily Anarchs in terms of numbers. It's just the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs part of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then you're talking about what you want VtM to be in your personal headspace and using it to dismiss people trying to talk about the actual game, if that is your reply to things like &quot;in the actual books, this person says&quot; and &quot;to change from being listed as a primary clan of one sect, to a primary clan of another sect, means at the most basic level there was enough of a shift to make that happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about &quot;always&quot; and start reaching back into the gameline over the years, and talk about the actual game, the game material itself has varied back and forth on the idea of &quot;how many Brujah are Anarchs.&quot; There's various material back over the years just straight up talking about the Brujah as a Camarilla clan as much as there is that goes another way, and not with the asterisk of &quot;because the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs as part of the Camarilla.&quot; Just third person objective listed or otherwise talked about as a Camarilla clan. So that comes off as &quot;so long as I ignore anything that says something not in line with my views, here is what the situation is.&quot;<br /> <br /> People are trying to talk about the published game material for the game Vampire the Masquerade, in this case 5th edition, and their reactions and opinions to it. You seem to only want to reply with this sort of thing. That material that disagrees with your perspective exists, does not make it not exist for disagreeing with you.<br /> <br /> Or, alternatively, page reference from something from Vampire the Masquerade 5th edition actually, directly stating that the Brujah have always been primarily Anarchs in terms of numbers? I'd be fine with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T18:50:50-07:00","id":1485069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485063#post1485063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're talking about what you want VtM to be in your personal headspace and using it to dismiss people trying to talk about the actual game</div> </div> </div> </div>MarkK, you DID know that the Camarilla considered Anarchs part of the Camarilla, right?<br /> <br /> This isn't me making up things.<br /> <br /> This was a long established part of the setting and a major reason that they were tolerated. It's part of the Convention of Thorns that they were part of the Camarilla and was illegal for the Princes to persecute them because they were Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Them being cast out with the Brujah is a big change.<br /> <br /> This is not new or an interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't previously said they had to make sacrifices. You said consistently and repeatedly that they made a genius move without any downside they wouldn't do anyway, and you said it was supported by the books, which it isn't. It is a generous interpretation of what lies beyond the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you persuaded me that it wasn't perfect as a move. Which I thought was your goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlso, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> said, the whole thing is about the Lasombra fleeing to Camarilla cities. The books do <u><b>not</b></u>, by any stretch, support the idea that the Lasombra rebuilt their power bases in the territory vacated by the Sabbat, they consistently state that the Lasombra are fleeing for Camarilla cities. So they <b>are </b>leaving their things behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are fleeing from their territories but in a modernized economy, it's not like their bank accounts and investments will be effected. The Lasombra might be leaving behind big troves of treasure if you consider that but if they have any wealth, it's almost certainly involved in non-material assets. The Lasombra also hold vast reach over the Church as its established and their loisses are minimal because if they'd stayed, they would have lost their influence anyway because the Sabbat were abandoning their cities no matter what.<br /> <br /> Sierra Burace is an example of a Lasombra who saves her personal fortune by joining the Camarilla because her defection allows her to bring her hotel chain into the Camarilla where she's protected by their ifnluence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No one objects that the defection was, given the circumstances, a good option. What's being argued is that the terms of the defection are badly written and definitely not the best any of the sides could have created and agreed upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you have handled the defection? Serious question.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear alternative ideas and often incorporate changes in my game. Mind you, I've stated many times I mostly prefer the handling of V5 as done by OPP than White Wolf as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-26-2022, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T19:19:12-07:00","id":1485071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MarkK, you DID know that the Camarilla considered Anarchs part of the Camarilla, right?<br /> <br /> This isn't me making up things.<br /> <br /> This was a long established part of the setting and a major reason that they were tolerated. It's part of the Convention of Thorns that they were part of the Camarilla and was illegal for the Princes to persecute them because they were Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Them being cast out with the Brujah is a big change.<br /> <br /> This is not new or an interpretation. </div> </div> </div>In no way does this reply to anything I said.<br /> <br /> You said this, as part of an effort to claim there was no real significant shift in Brujah numbers in terms of the sect notation change, that any Brujah who considered themselves actually Camarilla were not a significant departure from it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Really, they just expelled most of the ANARCHS from the Camarilla.</i> </div> </div> </div>Finding this odd, given the way certain 5th ed content presents itself, I said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is noted in the Camarilla book by Damian that enough non Anarch Brujah left the Camarilla to put a dent in various cities Primogen councils and reduce the Camarilla's boots on the ground strength in such places. The idea that but some sprinkling of Cam Brujah left does not bear out. Enough Brujah went in full to the Anarchs that were not Anarchs before that the Brujah are now considered a primary Anarch clan, as opposed to a clan where a bunch of them are Anarchs. That last part is just.. the Brujah being noted as one of the Anarch clans now, that's just sheer logistics. For that to be the case it has to mean that enough Brujah that were not anarchs before, became anarchs, to tip the scale that way. </div> </div> </div>You, in response, said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my perspective, the Brujah have always been primarily Anarchs in terms of numbers. It's just the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs part of the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>I, directly quoting this statement, said this, commenting on this statement:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you're talking about what you want VtM to be in your personal headspace and using it to dismiss people trying to talk about the actual game, if that is your reply to things like &quot;in the actual books, this person says&quot; and &quot;to change from being listed as a primary clan of one sect, to a primary clan of another sect, means at the most basic level there was enough of a shift to make that happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about &quot;always&quot; and start reaching back into the gameline over the years, and talk about the actual game, the game material itself has varied back and forth on the idea of &quot;how many Brujah are Anarchs.&quot; There's various material back over the years just straight up talking about the Brujah as a Camarilla clan as much as there is that goes another way, and not with the asterisk of &quot;because the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs as part of the Camarilla.&quot; Just third person objective listed or otherwise talked about as a Camarilla clan. So that comes off as &quot;so long as I ignore anything that says something not in line with my views, here is what the situation is.&quot;<br /> <br /> People are trying to talk about the published game material for the game Vampire the Masquerade, in this case 5th edition, and their reactions and opinions to it. You seem to only want to reply with this sort of thing. That material that disagrees with your perspective exists, does not make it not exist for disagreeing with you.<br /> <br /> Or, alternatively, page reference from something from Vampire the Masquerade 5th edition actually, directly stating that the Brujah have always been primarily Anarchs in terms of numbers? I'd be fine with that. </div> </div> </div>Nothing you have now said responds to these words in any way I can parse. It reads mostly like some kind of attempted topic change instead of responding to the request I have made in the face of your claims about the Brujah &quot;always&quot; having been a predominantly Anarch clan, and that, as a result, there was no significant change in their numbers as far as non Anarch Brujah leaving the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Do you no longer want to discuss the claim you have made that the Brujah have always been portrayed as majority Anarch and that as a result few of the Brujah who left the Camarilla were actually Camarilla? Saying &quot;the Camarilla considered Anarchs part of the Camarilla&quot; does not actually address the claim you made, it splits it into pieces to seemingly try and ignore the parts you no longer wish to discuss. Or at least, that's how it reads.<br /> <br /> It's also odd to read that you would ask me that question you did at all as your reply, did you gloss over the part of my post where I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's various material back over the years just straight up talking about the Brujah as a Camarilla clan <b>as much as there is that goes another way</b>, and not with the asterisk of &quot;because the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs as part of the Camarilla.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I have now bolded the relevant part, it seems you missed where I said that there has been material in the gameline previously both for and against the idea of Brujah as mostly Anarch. That's the only way the question you seem to gloss over the entirety of my post with feels possible to ask.<br /> <br /> I am attempting to talk to you about the claim you are making that &quot;the Brujah were a mostly Anarch clan anyway and the Brujah who mostly left were Anarchs anyway&quot;, itself based on your effort to claim that by and large only the Anarch Brujah left/were kicked the Camarilla in the 5th edition plot, and that the majority of the Brujah were never really Camarilla in the first place, the Camarilla only thought so. You are attempting to claim there was no real shift in the Clan's numbers in the Anarchs. In response to that I noted things like the Brujah being noted in various previous places in the game's history as a Camarilla clan from overall notation without the asterisk you insist on, and, ultimately somewhat more importantly, even simply various details actually present in 5th edition that we can look at. Because after all, if 5th does anything, it's play pretty selectively with previous VtM material anyway.<br /> <br /> Thus, as related to that claim, I have particularly asked where in 5th edition it actually says anything you are saying about that the Brujah were already majority Anarch anyway, and that as connected mostly the Brujah who left the Camarilla were already Anarchs anyway, in actual words.<br /> <br /> Your claim is that the Brujah were &quot;always&quot; predominantly Anarch and that as a result, there was no real shift when Brujah left for the Camarilla. I have noted that in previous VtM, that has only been sometimes the case in a given book that brings up that Brujah or Camarilla, and in other cases, they are not referred to that way. As though VtM is not, what's the word, all that consistent, but that doesn't mean any material you don't want to be right, never happened. I have otherwise thus asked where in 5th, despite otherwise talking about Brujah leaving the Camarilla, as though they were fully Camarilla Brujah, leaving the Camarilla, to join the Anarchs instead, it instead says the things you say.<br /> <br /> I would ask that if you're going to reply to this, to please reply to the things I have actually said, and the claims you have made that you can be quoted on making. If you can't, I'm not sure what the point would be of doing so.<br /> <br /> I will be as clear as I can. I am talking about what comes off as denying that there was a significant shift in 5th ed in the numbers of Brujah who were Anarchs, due to Camarilla Brujah now becoming Anarchs. I am, in commenting on the implausibility of that, pointing to the way some things in V5 are framed. I am talking about the idea that in fact there were a significant number of Camarilla Brujah, who were Camarilla, not &quot;Anarchs who the Camarilla stupidly believed were Camarilla&quot;, who left the Camarilla in V5 as part of the Brujah becoming an Anarch primary clan.<br /> <br /> If the only thing you can say is &quot;well previously it worked like this&quot;, I have already in fact replied &quot;yes, and previously it also sometimes didn't&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-26-2022, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T20:13:06-07:00","id":1485075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485037#post1485037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not for nothing, but while not the world's biggest fan of the Sabbat, there was more to do with them in V20 than play them as moustache twirling villains, and we've seen a hojillion threads at this point of fans of the Sabbat going into such things.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my view, it is ultimately more constructive to discussion to not assume they were bald faced lying when they say they do want you to play them and to simply consider how successful or not they were at the idea that they kept the clan playable. You can at least squint and see what they would have been thinking. You can then note why that didn't in practice actually work out, but I think it's reasonable to believe that some kind of try was made.</div> </div> </div> </div>1-of course, i'm simplifying for argument sake. Sabbat can be tragic heroes, camp villains, or political masterminds, However, you can't deny they make some of the worst neighbours. <br /> 2-V5 was made by a group of people. Dev A might have earnestly wanted x, but after politicking and compromise/other sections being written, we get Y or Z. I don't think Dev A's a liar, I just think his perspective might not apply to the whole team given the results we see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T22:38:35-07:00","id":1485078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485071#post1485071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing you have now said responds to these words in any way I can parse. It reads mostly like some kind of attempted topic change instead of responding to the request I have made in the face of your claims about the Brujah &quot;always&quot; having been a predominantly Anarch clan, and that, as a result, there was no significant change in their numbers as far as non Anarch Brujah leaving the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Do you no longer want to discuss the claim you have made that the Brujah have always been portrayed as majority Anarch and that as a result few of the Brujah who left the Camarilla were actually Camarilla? Saying &quot;the Camarilla considered Anarchs part of the Camarilla&quot; does not actually address the claim you made, it splits it into pieces to seemingly try and ignore the parts you no longer wish to discuss. Or at least, that's how it reads.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, I'm clearly misconstruing what you are saying. Is what you're asking about whether or not the Brujah being not a majority Anarch? This is sincere as I'm just making sure that what you're having a problem with is my claim that they are not the majority of the clan. In which case, that is something that I believe has been established by the Brujah Clanbooks where the two guides to the Clan heavily emphasize that the Neonate population and Ancilla populations are defined by Rebellion against the Status Quo. I did not understand that you were objecting to the idea of the Brujah being majority anarch and apologize becasue I didn't understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have now bolded the relevant part, it seems you missed where I said that there has been material in the gameline previously both for and against the idea of Brujah as mostly Anarch. That's the only way the question you seem to gloss over the entirety of my post with feels possible to ask. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's on me. I did not understand your question and apologize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am attempting to talk to you about the claim you are making that &quot;the Brujah were a mostly Anarch clan anyway and the Brujah who mostly left were Anarchs anyway&quot;, itself based on your effort to claim that by and large only the Anarch Brujah left/were kicked the Camarilla in the 5th edition plot, and that the majority of the Brujah were never really Camarilla in the first place, the Camarilla only thought so. You are attempting to claim there was no real shift in the Clan's numbers in the Anarchs. In response to that I noted things like the Brujah being noted in various previous places in the game's history as a Camarilla clan from overall notation without the asterisk you insist on, and, ultimately somewhat more importantly, even simply various details actually present in 5th edition that we can look at. Because after all, if 5th does anything, it's play pretty selectively with previous VtM material anyway. </div> </div> </div>No, the established status of the Camarilla in both 1st, 2nd, and 3rd edition is that the Camarilla is composed of the Anarchs and the Loyalists (for lack of a better term than the Camarilla). There is an independent Anarch free State but the Anarchs are members of the Camarilla and sunject to their laws until the events of 5th Edition.<br /> <br /> 5th Edition establishes the Anarchs as being no longer part of the Camarilla as part of the changes of the setting and they have expelled the Brujah and Gangrel Clans (the Gangrel in 3rd Edition). Both of which are recognized as Anarch Clans now alongside the Ministry. So in 5th Edition, both the Brujah and Gangrel are now majority Anarch Clans because they are the primary Clans of the Anarchs as recognized in the Anarch book.<br /> <br /> Again, my apologies, as I clearly did not understand your well-written post and I was confused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thus, as related to that claim, I have particularly asked where in 5th edition it actually says anything you are saying about that the Brujah were already majority Anarch anyway, and that as connected mostly the Brujah who left the Camarilla were already Anarchs anyway, in actual words. </div> </div> </div>Thank you, THIS I can answer and apologize for not doing it further.<br /> <br /> CLANBOOK: BRUJAH REVISED, PAGE 37:<br /> <br /> <b>Iconoclasts</b><br /> <br /> <i>In the modern nights, most Brujah<br /> probably fall into the iconoclast archetype,<br /> or at least they have over the past<br /> few decades. Social upheaval has long been<br /> a feature of the human condition \u2014 what<br /> is history but a collection of problems and<br /> people\u2019s resolutions of them? All Kindred<br /> were human at some point. To simplify<br /> the concept, iconoclasts are the most<br /> rebellious Brujah, quick to rally to any<br /> cause that espouses change. Many join<br /> anarch factions, hoping to bring Kindred<br /> social conventions up to date. They tend<br /> to be young, vigorous, and shortsighted<br /> \u2014 agitated iconoclasts happily incite riots,<br /> heedless of the fact that their own havens<br /> might be destroyed.</i><br /> <br /> Does this help?<br /> <br /> But yes, as much as I am apologist for a lot of V5's changes and ideas, I also note that the changes are done with a very blatant disregard for the past continuity and I wouldn't be nearly as interested in it if not for Beckett's Jyhad Diary and OPP's supplements that do their best to &quot;fix&quot; what I perceive as massive issues in the metaplot.<br /> <br /> I am less a fan of V5's supplements than I am of the world depicted in CHICAGO BY NIGHT 5th Edition and its supplements and CULT OF THE BLOOD GODS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-27-2022, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T23:56:24-07:00","id":1485083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485058#post1485058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my perspective, the Brujah have always been primarily Anarchs in terms of numbers. It's just the Camarilla stupidly considered all Anarchs part of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>On paper the Camarilla always claimed that they were the universal vampire organization and that every vampire in the world was part of the Camarilla. This made some sense since the only real goal for the Camarilla was to keep knowledge of vampires away from humanity. All of the Traditions and rules were simply there to reinforce the Masquerade and to prevent conflict between vampires that would eventually spill across to humanity.<br /> <br /> Of course in practice, you had vampires like the Sabbat who were opposed to the Camarilla, or groups like the Anarchs who rejected the Camarilla and you had vampires in other parts of the world that had never even heard of the Camarilla. Still, the idea was that any vampire from any clan or bloodline from anywhere in the world could show up in a Camarilla city, and they'd be treated like any other member of the Camarilla provided they followed the Traditions. Ultimately the Camarilla was formed to be an inclusive organization. So Anarchs were a part of it, but that wasn't stupid, that was intentional.<br /> <br /> Ultimately driving other vampires and geographies out of the sect just makes it harder for the Camarilla to quickly respond to Masquerade breaches. And again, the Camarilla was created under the concept that &quot;vampires need to stand together or get individually burned to death by humanity&quot; like they did during the Inquisition. It's really only been in 5th edition that the Camarilla has gone more from inclusive to exclusive, and <i>that's</i> kind of stupid because now it's just going to be that much harder to deal with a breach of the Masquerade when it occurs in territory or by vampires that the Camarilla has officially disavowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T23:57:24-07:00","id":1485084,"title":"","content":"So I think it's fair to say 'many Brujah were part of the Anarchs when Anarchs were part of the Camarilla', based on the text above. 'Many' is the wording used in Cb:BruRev, and that's vague enough to allow you to set that number according to the needs of your chronicle. In that sense, those Brujah are Schr\u00f6dinger's Anarchs -- both members of the Camarilla and not members of the Camarilla, depending on how you look at it. And you can decide whether many is more than half, a third, a quarter, a sizeable minority, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T00:08:30-07:00","id":1485085,"title":"","content":"I concede I was misreading the text and that MarkK is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T01:52:00-07:00","id":1485094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485083#post1485083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On paper the Camarilla always claimed that they were the universal vampire organization and that every vampire in the world was part of the Camarilla. This made some sense since the only real goal for the Camarilla was to keep knowledge of vampires away from humanity. All of the Traditions and rules were simply there to reinforce the Masquerade and to prevent conflict between vampires that would eventually spill across to humanity.<br /> <br /> Of course in practice, you had vampires like the Sabbat who were opposed to the Camarilla, or groups like the Anarchs who rejected the Camarilla and you had vampires in other parts of the world that had never even heard of the Camarilla. Still, the idea was that any vampire from any clan or bloodline from anywhere in the world could show up in a Camarilla city, and they'd be treated like any other member of the Camarilla provided they followed the Traditions. Ultimately the Camarilla was formed to be an inclusive organization. So Anarchs were a part of it, but that wasn't stupid, that was intentional.<br /> <br /> Ultimately driving other vampires and geographies out of the sect just makes it harder for the Camarilla to quickly respond to Masquerade breaches. And again, the Camarilla was created under the concept that &quot;vampires need to stand together or get individually burned to death by humanity&quot; like they did during the Inquisition. It's really only been in 5th edition that the Camarilla has gone more from inclusive to exclusive, and <i>that's</i> kind of stupid because now it's just going to be that much harder to deal with a breach of the Masquerade when it occurs in territory or by vampires that the Camarilla has officially disavowed.</div> </div> </div> </div> The new exclusivity of the sect also subtly undermines the proposed primary conflict of v5 by removing a point of contention with the anarchs. Under v5 its completly fine for territories to exist outside of carmarilla authority.<br /> <br /> I get they.where trying to set the sect up as a sort of snooty 1% have vs have nots but it's even that falls apart when you think on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T04:19:57-07:00","id":1485101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485094#post1485094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The new exclusivity of the sect also subtly undermines the proposed primary conflict of v5 by removing a point of contention with the anarchs. Under v5 its completly fine for territories to exist outside of carmarilla authority.<br /> <br /> I get they.where trying to set the sect up as a sort of snooty 1% have vs have nots but it's even that falls apart when you think on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, because you can't have a snooty 1% with no 99% to lord over. Even if one considers the humans to be that 99% rather than Low Clans, you still need a military to enforce your will. Otherwise you're just a bunch of helpless aristocrats waiting impotently for the rebels to literally walk through the door unopposed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T04:58:44-07:00","id":1485102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485101#post1485101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, because you can't have a snooty 1% with no 99% to lord over. Even if one considers the humans to be that 99% rather than Low Clans, you still need a military to enforce your will. Otherwise you're just a bunch of helpless aristocrats waiting impotently for the rebels to literally walk through the door unopposed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It probably doesn't help that the carmarilla actually covers a far larger base of vampiric population the setting acknowlages, you've got roughly 2 rich guy clans 2-3 disenfranchised clans by severity of flaw, 2 refugee clans and 2 clans in complete free fall and by free fall I mean &quot;we might be a bloodline in terms of numbers&quot; shortly.<br /> <br /> <br /> They kind of work in the context of 1st world vs 3rd world circa early post Soviet 1990's (lol) but they're loasy model for 22 global politics and vtm shies away from that anyway because of its focus on the 'street'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T09:26:27-07:00","id":1485116,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that it comes off like a built in goal with the V5 Camarilla that it isn't to be some carefully thought out (by which I mean, the writers carefully thinking out how it would need to function to reconcile with detail x, y or z) tangible entity that functions within internal setting constraints. It's mostly to be a thematic antagonist punching bag for the Anarchs as a commentary on society's ills. So you can say &quot;but logically&quot; or even &quot;but your own writing now says&quot;, it's just, even if pointed out, I doubt that would get anything but a reply of &quot;yeah, see how short sighted and unthinking the Camarilla are now?&quot; as an intended point. The individual details that seem glaring to you, like for instance a supposed sect of elites having multiple clans of wildly varying situations, come off as completely irrelevant to them.<br /> <br /> If there's one thing you can say about V5, it's that serving the meta themes and images comes first, and thinking everything else out comes second.<br /> <br /> Listen, it's not like taking this approach always fails. By which I mean, do you enjoy Baz Luhrman movies? (I absolutely do). That is a guy who is one million percent not thinking about how something sensibly comes together or reconciles with its own plot construction, even just from the details of his own writing. He is telling some story of broad, powerful themes and images with lush, lavish imagery and set pieces, and not one where he cares if you get hung up on whether the specifics made any damn sense. He gets away with this on sheer, impossible, incredible, grab you by the face, style. And if there has ever been a game that is style first, it is VtM.<br /> <br /> Of course, to put it lightly, Vampire the Masquerade 5th edition books are not the movies of Baz Luhrman (also even his movies don't *always* work, a few of them just collapse under their own weight or can't quite paper over some baffling thing/terrible decision).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-27-2022, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T12:06:15-07:00","id":1485126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485116#post1485116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that it comes off like a built in goal with the V5 Camarilla that it isn't to be some carefully thought out (by which I mean, the writers carefully thinking out how it would need to function to reconcile with detail x, y or z) tangible entity that functions within internal setting constraints. It's mostly to be a thematic antagonist punching bag for the Anarchs as a commentary on society's ills. So you can say &quot;but logically&quot; or even &quot;but your own writing now says&quot;, it's just, even if pointed out, I doubt that would get anything but a reply of &quot;yeah, see how short sighted and unthinking the Camarilla are now?&quot; as an intended point. The individual details that seem glaring to you, like for instance a supposed sect of elites having multiple clans of wildly varying situations, come off as completely irrelevant to them.<br /> <br /> If there's one thing you can say about V5, it's that serving the meta themes and images comes first, and thinking everything else out comes second.<br /> <br /> Listen, it's not like taking this approach always fails. By which I mean, do you enjoy Baz Luhrman movies? (I absolutely do). That is a guy who is one million percent not thinking about how something sensibly comes together or reconciles with its own plot construction, even just from the details of his own writing. He is telling some story of broad, powerful themes and images with lush, lavish imagery and set pieces, and not one where he cares if you get hung up on whether the specifics made any damn sense. He gets away with this on sheer, impossible, incredible, grab you by the face, style. And if there has ever been a game that is style first, it is VtM.<br /> <br /> Of course, to put it lightly, Vampire the Masquerade 5th edition books are not the movies of Baz Luhrman (also even his movies don't *always* work, a few of them just collapse under their own weight or can't quite paper over some baffling thing/terrible decision).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see your mindset and appreciate ithere but it sort of damns the setting with faint praise.<br /> <br /> For the record I'm not a fan of baz Lurhman movies lol. Except romeo and Juliet whoever wrote the script for that movie should be applauded since it let's him work on aesthetic instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-27-2022, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T12:33:48-07:00","id":1485131,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey, I'm not saying it works effectively in this case, I'm just saying how it comes off by this point and how the mindset behind it feels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T12:59:10-07:00","id":1485134,"title":"","content":"I'm going to continue my, &quot;I like V5 but really only OPP's V5.&quot; Which I think I've probably beaten like a dead horse but I'm going to continue saying because I think their Chicago by Night 5E is one of the best supplements ever created.<br /> <br /> Basically, OPP solves the issue by having Anarchs and Camarilla forces sharing the same city as well as competing for resources rather than having &quot;Anarch territory, Blood Cult territory, Camarilla territory.&quot; Kevin Jackson rules over the &quot;good' parts of Chicago but the Anarchs are powerful and numerous enough that they have their own territory so they can't be beaten. You then have vampires who are part of the Camarilla or Anarchs who don't actually CARE and just want to get along to get along.<br /> <br /> It's not ENTIRELY original and strongly reflects the set up in BLOODLINES that was actually a pretty unique situation. There you had a Prince and his enforcers but the Anarchs were powerful as well as in rebellion against the Prince so each side had territory within LA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T13:36:01-07:00","id":1485140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485116#post1485116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's one thing you can say about V5, it's that serving the meta themes and images comes first, and thinking everything else out comes second..</div> </div> </div> </div>My lord, you've just described one of the worst ideas i can think of for game design...<br /> <br /> PS, Strictly Ballroom and Romeo + Juliet were fun, but in the remember about them once a decade kinda way. Checking IMBD, all the rest of his films are the ones i looked at and thought looked like overindulgant nonsense. Never really heard his name much as a director...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T16:39:41-07:00","id":1485147,"title":"","content":"I will talk some specifics that relate to my actual irl job, plus answer a direct request. Otherwise I think the matter was debated more than enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485069#post1485069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they are fleeing from their territories but in a modernized economy, it's not like their bank accounts and investments will be effected.</div> </div> </div> </div>They will, specially if you consider how vampires own things (through proxies).<br /> <br /> First, most wealth in the world does not exist as money, it exists as a long list of assets, specially as property and real estate. While you can easily transfer their formal ownership in paper, the actual assets exist as physical objects, often immobile and too frequently hard to transport. That's true for any millionaire and even more so for those who operate outside the law, as such assets can have their actual control and ownership unbound from legal possession.<br /> <br /> Second, investments are... complex. You can't simply liquidate or transfer them at your leisure without loss, sometimes at all. Realizing loss is one of the worst things you can do, and you usually have to when liquidating pronto due to an unforeseen emergency. Some you can't withdraw from earlier than agreed upon. Some are extremely volatile and can cause actual loss (not only lose the whole invested money, but also end up with debt after that) if you can't follow through.<br /> <br /> But the biggest issue is that for influence and direct control, <i>specially</i>the kind of control the Lasombra like, nothing beats proximity. As a vampire your real asset isn't to nominally own something, but to be able to direct how it works (or not). Nominating and <b>Dominating</b> CEOs, collecting protection in money and blood, and so on. <i>The eye of the master fattens the horse</i>, and if this isn't completely true for modern <b>legit</b> businesses, it is completely so for most <b>non-legit</b> ones, and doubly for the likes of the undead as described in VtM.<br /> <br /> Add proxies to the equation and things get a lot worse. It's not <b>just</b> about accessing your assets anymore, but accessing intermediaries that nominally own those assets or directly manage them. If the proxy is cut off, then you have problem. If another vampire take hold of your proxy, then you also have problems. Those that stay behind can destroy, cripple, or achieve effective informal control, or steal the control from you, with little you can do from afar since you don't have direct legal ownership of anything.<br /> <br /> Now, this isn't to say that every situation is equal and it will never go well. As any complex situation, you can have a lot of outcomes between profit and total bankruptcy. Some Lasombra may have came out of that better than they were before, and a very few may be quite a lot better as they took unusual opportunities. But to address the group in general we have to fallback to averages, and it is unlikely that the clan as a whole didn't lost a lot.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear: my intent here isn't to &quot;beat a dead horse&quot; or anything like that, but to explain some of the nuances involved in the actual process of transferring wealth for whomever wants to use it and/or start from this to learn more. I wish I could have got a job in my actual original academic area, but since I got employed in a bank, I really learned the ins and outs of the financial system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485069#post1485069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you have handled the defection? Serious question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's get from the point they were in the actual setting, regardless of my opinion in this point: the Camarilla ditched two clans and is on the lookout for wealth and strength, the Lasombra defectors know they have to leave the Sabbat pronto and with protection for the time being.<br /> <br /> As much as they can boast and hide from each other during the exchanges and meetings, they know each other's basic needs at least, but also that they need to keep each other at arm's length. They need some guarantees against each other. But also need each other specifically even more so for the fact that they don't: the Lasombra going to the Anarchs is still plainly on the table, and while no one at it wants that option, if they can't reach an agreement it will be it (hence why asking for or accepting genocide isn't an option).<br /> <br /> Some back and forth and several nights later, the Lasombra offer the most prized possession: knowledge. They'll teach the Tremere the Sabbat Ritae, so they can together devise countermeasures for some of them, above all the Vinculum. They need a way to strip their own Vinculum and, they know it, be Bound to some Camarilla members. That's a guaranteed outcome for some, no reason to fight it. Other Ritae go as a bonus, even if the negotiation fail it is now in their best interest to teach the Camarilla the secrets of the Sabbat and let them fight each other.<br /> <br /> In exchange, the Lasombra demand some specific positions. Nothing too high, but positions meant to ease the process of defection. A Justicar of their own, an Archon under two or three other Justicars, a liaison to the Tremere to discuss matters of Abyss Mysticism and another to the Inner Council acting as military advisor against the Sabbat, then insist that at least some important cities get to have a member of the clan at any position the local Prince wants, preferably as enforcers. Those are all good positions to negotiate because they're politically dead, but key to ease things up and make the defection safer for the clan as a whole. Others will try later to acquire true power, they can't push too much now.<br /> <br /> Finally whatever comes from the Vinculum-Breaking ritual is prepared and the actual process of defection begin. The Camarilla will ease the transference or recuperation of assets, but will confiscate most of it whenever it can, this is the actual price to be paid. Here is where Princes will most exert their individual policies, some may demand only a token tax and offer ample help, others may go for it all. Some Princes may still add to the demands, and most will offer &quot;tax exemptions&quot; in exchange of staked Sabbat elders, enough to force the Lasombra to burn bridges, but usually not enough to jeopardize the whole process, a single important Sabbat elder buys out entry for several clan members (or only one really rich and powerful).<br /> <br /> Personally I would make the Vinculum-Breaking somewhat unreliable on the Bonding side, it makes the Vinculum break as intended, but sometimes the Bonding protection remains for a time. The Tremere is aware of that, but being unable to tell with certainty who's Bonded and who's not plays well for both sides, as otherwise they would have to debate who'll be subject to the Blood Bond. Now it is hard to betray each other as they don't know who'll ultimately play in which side, better to just get along. After a while I would have a similar process for the reclamation of abandoned Sabbat cities. The defection itself would have some skirmishes, but would mostly be as silent and quick as possible, without much time dedicated to hunting people and with many Lasombra being subject to the breaking of the Vinculum to join the defectors (or not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485140#post1485140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My lord, you've just described one of the worst ideas i can think of for game design...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, imo even V5 is far from the worse in this regard. The worse is <i>Cyberpunk 2020</i>. Never liked it, and I'm a fan of Gibson's work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T17:29:09-07:00","id":1485152,"title":"","content":"My idea for the defection is the King's and Queens of shadow descretly slink across during the gehenna war/2nd inquisition after years of secret negotiations with the price being an obscene amount of laundered cash and assets. Majority of the clan remain Sabbat but carmarilla numbers are substantially boosted at a 60/10/30 ratio between sects. Les amis noir now acts as a neutral ground for the keepers and thus, a strictly kept secret. The key point was this being a premeditated move with careful planning as opposed to a TV soap style plot twist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-27-2022, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T11:10:24-07:00","id":1485195,"title":"","content":"You know, if Oblivion's thematically supposed to take a toll on your will to live/exist/resist the beast and care and blah, I think it already used to have a mechanic that could've worked; willpower costs.<br /> <br /> Instead of stains, why couldn't some powers just have made you roll for willpower damage or something? I've forgoten the specifics of V5's mechanics by this point, but isn't willpower potentially used in rolls to stop the beast interfering with your behaviour and potentially sabotaging your humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T13:08:05-07:00","id":1485205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485195#post1485195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if Oblivion's thematically supposed to take a toll on your will to live/exist/resist the beast and care and blah, I think it already used to have a mechanic that could've worked; willpower costs.<br /> <br /> Instead of stains, why couldn't some powers just have made you roll for willpower damage or something? I've forgoten the specifics of V5's mechanics by this point, but isn't willpower potentially used in rolls to stop the beast interfering with your behaviour and potentially sabotaging your humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good argument the Lasombra got overly nerfed all round.<br /> <br /> The Technology Flaw is crippling.<br /> <br /> Why also cripple the already-downgraded Obternation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T17:08:07-07:00","id":1485231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485205#post1485205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a good argument the Lasombra got overly nerfed all round.<br /> <br /> The Technology Flaw is crippling.<br /> <br /> Why also cripple the already-downgraded Obternation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously the new Flaw makes them perfectly suited to... be in the Camarilla and follow the new rules.<br /> <br /> Hooray...?<br /> <br /> As it is now, Obtenebration just don't need any extra costs, period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T23:04:12-07:00","id":1485262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485205#post1485205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a good argument the Lasombra got overly nerfed all round.<br /> <br /> The Technology Flaw is crippling.<br /> <br /> Why also cripple the already-downgraded Obternation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potence is weaker<br /> Dominate is considerably weaker<br /> The Technology flaw is inappropriate, and makes them weaker<br /> <br /> If you wanted to play a sauve, sexy sociopath who thinks he/she is a cut above the rest, clearly Lasombra is no longer a valid option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T06:11:45-07:00","id":1485278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485205#post1485205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why also cripple the already-downgraded Obternation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Lasombra already so wrecked it makes no difference? (imo)<br /> <br /> (I also legitimately forgot Oblivion included Obtenebration for a moment there. Probably selective memory. <i>Necromancy</i> occasionally had a willpower cost, which was what I was thinking of.)<br /> <br /> Tech flaw is ridiculous, the concept of no reflection or dead reflections is much cooler. The removal of the Sabbat and the... (uh, I'm struggling with words today?) insult(?) to the Lasombra Antitribu is not something I look on kindly, to be very mild about it. I do <i>not</i> like Oblivion*. But thematically, Oblivion's<i> intended</i> to destroy its users, does the method of destruction matter? If you don't want to risk destroying your character with it, you wouldn't use it. At least willpower is easier to recover than humanity.<br /> <br /> Whether it was functional or not was not something I factored into my thoughts, it doesn't affect me either which way. It was just the theme they seem to be aiming for and it occured to me that the nihilism and self-destruction manifest in Oblivion (the one at the bottom of the Underworld) tainting its user can be reflected in low willpower (and leans into vampires such as the Lasombra and Giovanni favouring driven candidates (who have high willpower)).<br /> <br /> *well, ok, I like it as its own thing in theme, I don't like it replacing Obtenebration and Necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-29-2022, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T07:28:44-07:00","id":1485287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485278#post1485278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But thematically, Oblivion's<i> intended</i> to destroy its users, does the method of destruction matter? If you don't want to risk destroying your character with it, you wouldn't use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, because this is a game and the power is meant to be used, specially when it is a standard power for a standard clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T08:11:47-07:00","id":1485290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485287#post1485287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, because this is a game and the power is meant to be used, specially when it is a standard power for a standard clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean it doesn't <i>matter,</i> objectively, I meant it doesn't matter to <i>me. </i>It was being flippant about my stance on the matter. A standard power being uniquely destructive when the other clans don't have to deal with this is something I'd consider bad design choice, so ultimately, the choice between &quot;bad design choice A&quot; and &quot;bad design choice B&quot; when both ultimately have the same result is a nuance I (personally) disregard as not mattering.<br /> <br /> I just saw the thread, and had a passing thought about Necromancy's willpower cost and Oblivion's destructive themes that went &quot;huh, what if it caused willpower damage instead?&quot; that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-29-2022, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T11:31:48-07:00","id":1485306,"title":"","content":"I've noticed the thread seems to thread closer to lasombra focuses over hecteta. I'm curious if this is due to the heceta being one of the better written soft retcons of v5 or people just preferring lasombra in general.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it giovanni where historically a pretty rare play choice in my gaming circles although cappadocians where popular to the point people wanted to play them on modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T11:43:02-07:00","id":1485307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485306#post1485306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed the thread seems to thread closer to lasombra focuses over hecteta. I'm curious if this is due to the heceta being one of the better written soft retcons of v5 or people just preferring lasombra in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if we're going off-topic, but from what little I've seen, the Hecata is composed of several Clans and Bloodlines that were literally mortal (or immortal) enemies. The book Cults of the Blood Gods started with a story about how the Harbinger of Skulls nearly wiped out the Pisanob before cutting to a flashback of one surviving Pisanop gouging out a Harbinger's eyes. And then they're all having a nice family dinner. <br /> <br /> Between that and everyone in the new &quot;Clan&quot; suddenly replacing their original bloodline weaknesses to the Lamia's Kiss for unexplained (Watsonian) reasons, it sounds like their retcon was anything but &quot;soft.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T13:07:34-07:00","id":1485311,"title":"","content":"I think the bigger issue is something I mentioned earlier in the thread: The Lasombra are a Clan aligned with one of the major playable Sects. The Hecata are independents. Playing Hecata PCs is always going to be a bit of a hurdle because either they're going against the new &quot;Clan&quot; and throwing in with one of the big Sects, or they're outsiders in the local politics. This is even more on focus as the Banu Hakim and Ministry have both picked a side rather than staying independent Clans as well. With only the metaplot devastated Ravnos and Salubri to join them in this category, it makes the Hecata less appealing as PCs (and continues the trend of making players that want to play independent Clans in non-independent focused games red flags to a lot of STs).<br /> <br /> It's also a bit easier to make the case that the necromancer side of Oblivion at least gets you more than most Disciplines do via Ceremonies (though that logic isn't consistent vis a vis Blood Sorcery) and thus an increased cost might be perceived as &quot;worth it.&quot; Lasombra players that jut want to copy Obtenebration in V5 are the ones that are most impacted by the changes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T18:07:36-07:00","id":1485325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485306#post1485306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed the thread seems to thread closer to lasombra focuses over hecteta. I'm curious if this is due to the heceta being one of the better written soft retcons of v5 or people just preferring lasombra in general.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it giovanni where historically a pretty rare play choice in my gaming circles although cappadocians where popular to the point people wanted to play them on modern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the Hecata was better done than the Defection, that's all. The thread went in the direction of &quot;this was yet another punch on the Lasombra&quot; and, well, the Hecata has its problems, but nothing to the same degree.<br /> <br /> But I do think that making every &quot;Death Clan&quot; follow the same rules was a boring idea to say the least. And the core problem in the thread is pretty much the same for both.<br /> <br /> Although actually I think it is even worse theme-wise for the non-Giovanni derived Hecata, as they're even less linked to corruption and whatnot than either Giovanni or Lasombra (<i>arguably</i> the Nagaraja are next in the list).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485307#post1485307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if we're going off-topic, but from what little I've seen, the Hecata is composed of several Clans and Bloodlines that were literally mortal (or immortal) enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much, actually.<br /> <br /> Most of those bloodline are actually just <b>Giovanni</b> families: <i><b>Dunsirn</b></i>, <i><b>Pisanob</b></i>, <i><b>Puttanesca</b></i>, <i><b>Rossellini</b></i> and <i><b>Milliners</b></i> have all been a part of the <b>Giovanni</b> before, any previous relationship was just background. <b><i>Samedi</i></b> and <b><i>Nagaraja</i></b> never quite cared, being focused on their own thing and content on being left alone before, they wouldn't shy from a survival alliance.<br /> <br /> Then we get the surviving <b>Cappadocians</b>, but those are in a complex position. The thing is, since the <u>Feast of Folly</u> sentiments within the Cappadocians are complex. Different factions within the clan have a vendetta with different other factions within the clan, tied to a specific event in the past or another.<br /> <br /> So basically the process of formation of the Hecata let those factions have their sweet time with the surviving original offenders, which seems reasonable, and those are among the most reasonable bloodlines in the game's history, so it kinda works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T01:43:52-07:00","id":1485344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485325#post1485325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although actually I think it is even worse theme-wise for the non-Giovanni derived Hecata, as they're even less linked to corruption and whatnot than either Giovanni or Lasombra (<i>arguably</i> the Nagaraja are next in the list).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The cappadocians main probably has it worst on.this front I think, several of the clans historical abilities have nothing to do with the dark umbra full stop. Especially considering the powers that suppress vampirism. It also serves as a bit of a plot hole that the deeply curious cappadocians seemed oblivious to lasombra insights into their staple discipline.<br /> <br /> I tend to play heceta as more a series of non aggression pacts than anything the clan name is mostly a way of letting everyone save face with clan status. Several sub groups still discretly despise each other and Co operation is minimal. Anyone claiming to identify as heceta alone is lying.<br /> <br /> But yes you are right hecata is genrally better written, some people seem happy having more general death clan. Personally I'm a little annoyed they tripped the final hurdle by fusing harbingers and cappodicians and making all their powers mask based. If you're going to do this I'd like to be able to play a full blown unfiltered member of the origional clan of death rather than the 5 flavours of giovanni.<br /> <br /> Then again I got my 1st fictional crush serina from redemption back from the giovanni which improved my mood considerably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-30-2022, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T06:49:00-07:00","id":1485366,"title":"","content":"I think the Hecata work sort of like the Children of Osiris or Baali apostates. They're both a clan and a sect, but more like the latter than the former. I run them as a sect-posing-as-clan, where the cracks are obvious internally but less so externally, and where several factions actively hate each other.<br /> <br /> But in general, I think the Hecata thing of maiden/mother/crone (Cappadocian/Giovanni/Hecata or birth/death/rebirth) is quite fitting and thematically appropriate for a clan of death. It also helps that it was introduced in BJD in V20, so it was less of a surprise.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra suffer from their defection being even less logical than a bunch of clans who hate each other coming together for strength and power. That excuse nearly always works for vampires. But the Lasombra had the strength and power, and they gave it up because reasons. That doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T07:09:35-07:00","id":1485367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485344#post1485344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm a little annoyed they tripped the final hurdle by fusing harbingers and cappodicians and making all their powers mask based. If you're going to do this I'd like to be able to play a full blown unfiltered member of the origional clan of death rather than the 5 flavours of giovanni.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like every detail about their lore, and definitely do not like their mechanics, but then the question I was answering had more to do with the most offensive lore, not mechanics, and Lasombra's lore is the worse by far.<br /> <br /> To me the Hecata works ok as a non-aggression/mutual protection pact, and I'm even ok with them not hating each other that much. But I don't see much reason for them to be a &quot;sect&quot; in the sense of curbing members' participation on the other sects, and I will just ignore the unifying rules and have them be themselves.<br /> <br /> Not even posing as a clan seems interesting or necessary, at all. Being a mutual protection coalition is more than enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T08:08:38-07:00","id":1485373,"title":"","content":"V5 be all like, you're a vampire, an undead blood monster, we can think of two appropriate magics for that;<br /> Choose: <br /> DEATH MAGIC<br /> or <br /> BLOOD MAGIC<br /> <br /> We just want you to be absolutely sure that these are HORRIFYING disciplines because it's a HORROR game. <br /> PS: They both suck","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T08:49:43-07:00","id":1485381,"title":"","content":"I define a Clan by their descent from an Antediluvian. These bloodlines are all descended from Cappadocius, ergo they are a clan. I hate the dissolution of bloodline identity into the Giovanni, but don't object to the Hecata as a body. I reinterpret it as more of a Clanbook Cappadocian for the modern nights. &quot;Here's the clan of death; it has half a dozen distinct bloodlines all doing their own thing.&quot; It's not a sect, in the sense that it precludes loyalty to one of the main sects. It's a sort of Nosferatu &quot;Clan before Sect&quot; mentality. Except with more internal hatred and factionalism.<br /> <br /> Canonically, they are very much not a happy family. Some do want the alliance, others are trying to pick it apart at the seams and are only there by peer pressure (or refusing to take part).<br /> <br /> But I can believe they're all going along with it.<br /> I'm also just going to have to shove my inability to be concise under a spoiler tag.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Harbingers:</b> OK, so if I were a vampire, and I got locked in a cave and left to starve until I cannibalised my fellows, and then had to spend the next thousand years or so struggling to survive in purgatory/hell carrying that trauma and more, and then I got home and found out that, ironically, the rest of the clan - the guys who &quot;dad&quot; singled out as the &quot;good&quot; children he <i>wasn't</i> going to condemn to a horrifying death - had suffered and died while you, contrary to intentions, survived, the only tears I would shed would be tears of laughter.<br /> V5 says their issue with the Giovanni is not the deaths of their other clan mates but that they lost the opportunity to kill their &quot;father&quot; with their own hands, and I buy it.<br /> <br /> The attacks on the Pisanob are sometimes interpreted as vengeance on the Cappadocian Pisanob for selling out. It might be, but I also interpret it as them lashing out at those who were spared their abuse. I've found that experiences like the HoS' tends to foster resentment. I think they hate the Cappadocians just as much, if not more than the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> That's not to say everybody's ok with the Capapdocian genocide or that they're buddy-buddy with Venice now, but they got their revenge by proxy and most of them are not inclined to be pleasant people. If I recall, Cappadocius' call to Kaymalki was not for gathering all the most good and forgiving. Most are likely on Death and the Soul, not Humanity. Loads of people died? Boo hoo, that's called a research opportunity.<br /> <br /> They've only been back for a while, they're a tiny group out of touch with both the modern world and the kindred one. The Giovanni have the resources and connections they lack and they're exploitable right now. The alliance has benefits. Plus their loyalty to Lazarus who saved them and delivered their revenge, and he wants the reunion, so hey, they're in.<br /> <br /> <b>Samedi: </b>Pretty sure this is a business deal for them. The Samedi don't seem overly bothered by clan history or who hates who. They don't like the Giovanni, but they seem to have already had some manner of truce with them. Baron Samedi matters more than some prehistoric Anatolian dude (and they're descended from the Infitiores, so fuck him anyway), and the Baron has told his children that they're a branch of one of the 13 clans, so sure, whatever.<br /> They do business, and in return they get protection backing them up when somebody looks at their face and screams &quot;Masquerade breach.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Cappadocians:</b> This is the group I can see having the biggest problem with the reunion. But on the other hand, the surviving original Cappadocians are a small and persecuted number, and if they're not in on the treaty they're still fair game for murder by both the Giovanni and the HoS, while the Samedi have no reason to care. Safer to keep your enemies close while you regain the ability to walk in the open. Maybe fuck them over from the inside. It's not just a gathering of you and the Giovanni, it's a gathering of you and everyone else who hates them with the Giovanni in clear sight.<br /> <br /> <b>Giovanni: </b>The Minor - now Other - Families (except the Pisanob) may be able to play nice with the other bloodlines better than <i>The</i> Family. They weren't involved with the Conspiracy of Isaac or the Capapdocians and they all despise the Giovanni too. It's an alliance built to fuck over the Venetians, let them rule themselves, and it expanded their knowledge of necromancy.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni I see as the second hardest to reconcile, because they just lost a lot of standing. They're still the main bloodline. Rich, influential and powerful still, sure, but their cousins just took chunks of that away with them. I imagine they're ironically in the same situation as the Cappadocians they hunted - you sign onto this treaty, or everyone you've pissed off declares open season on you. They're powerful, but they've lost most of their elders and they're up against the 8+ other families (who all resent them), the Samedi (don't like 'em either), the Cappadocians (itching to kill them all), the Harbingers (Ancient Elders and Methuselahs), and also every single wraith and spectre they've ever pissed off.<br /> Peace treaty it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do not understand the Lamia anyway, so their motivation is whatever. They seem to do whatever the Cappadocians do. As far as my games are concerned, they're exstinct and the &quot;Seed of Lilith&quot; lives on in the Giovanni after Lamia's diablerie. The Nagaraja don't make sense to me either, but they're there, I suppose.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> tl;dr, I'd say the bloodlines have agreed to reunify the clan based on survival, and only the Giovanni (the Venetians, specifically), the Pisanob and the Cappadocians are really a significant risk to Clan cooperation. Harbingers are out of touch with the world and need the others' connections, the walking Masqerade breaches known as the Samedi get business and protection, the other families got independece from Venice, and the Giovanni and Cappadocians avoid having open season declared on them. Most importantly, they're not all killing each other in a massive civil war just yet.<br /> <br /> There are also probably some thousand-year-plan Methuselah metaplot shenanigans in the background.<br /> <br /> And while I don't like the exact handling, I do like that the Samedi and Cappadocians can be more in the spotlight as PCs without getting rid of the Giovanni, and that the various forms of Necromancy are a bit more accessible between the bloodlines (if you transplant the Hecata back to V20. Oblivion does not currently contain the full range and it made them extra edgy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-30-2022, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T16:14:58-07:00","id":1485424,"title":"","content":"My spin is i tend to run them as subtly leaning towards specific sects.<br /> <br /> Cappadocians-the cappadocians are slowly gravitating towards the Carmarilla. They're still bitter about the promise but historical links with the ventrue indicate they'll be formally confirmed as members of the sect at the next inner council meeting.<br /> <br /> Giovanni-giovanni remain independent alongside the piscanob, dunscirn and other families with the exception of the milliners.<br /> <br /> Harbingers and milliners have remained and defected to Sabbat respectively. <br /> <br /> Samedi-nominally mercenary independent but gravitating towards anarch as repeat customers.<br /> <br /> Nanaraja-ashirra for geographical reasons.<br /> <br /> Lamia- independent, lamia tend to resume their roles as protectors of the cappadicians and to a lesser degree, harbingers and samedia so are found in a number of sects. A number remain independent and are rumoured to directly serve the capuchin or whoever ate Augustus....<br /> <br /> Side note-everyone is very wary of the heceta due to recent events. Heceta are genrally less than forthcoming or contradictory when questioned.<br /> <br /> I think it allows for a playable necromancer options in all sect while maintaining flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-30-2022, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T16:17:29-07:00","id":1485425,"title":"","content":"I can buy the idea that most Cappadocians are happy enough with not being on the &quot;to kill&quot; list to let go everything else. At least they weren't in hell, and if they insist on the whole &quot;sins of the father&quot; thing they'll be just as guilty. Again, with the Giovanni elders that really pressed for their hunt killed in the process of formation of the Hecata, with Augustus being given a specially gruesome ritualistic end, it isn't all that unlikely that they feel avenged enough.<br /> <br /> The Lamia are weird, indeed, probably just following the Cappadocians. The Nagaraja are leaderless and clueless since Revised nuked their leadership, so they're all in for survival and whatever.<br /> <br /> But I actually have some sympathy for their original depiction, so I'm considering in my games to have the Nagaraja still in Enoch and/or now in contact with the Traditions or Disparate Alliance (they're actually an old Mage Craft and their Mages still existed until the Nuke).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:10:41-07:00","id":1485466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485425#post1485425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can buy the idea that most Cappadocians are happy enough with not being on the &amp;quot;to kill&amp;quot; list to let go everything else. At least they weren't in hell, and if they insist on the whole &amp;quot;sins of the father&amp;quot; thing they'll be just as guilty. Again, with the Giovanni elders that really pressed for their hunt killed in the process of formation of the Hecata, with Augustus being given a specially gruesome ritualistic end, it isn't all that unlikely that they feel avenged enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The way I tend to run it is cold acceptance. Neither is inclined to move against the other but both are genrally unwilling to support or assist one another. Tolerance in the literal sense rather than modern, I like as a plot point and obvious source of conflict. For example I ran a short mystery were a giovanni anchilli went missing and naturally the first suspect is the cappadocian eldar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T03:49:43-07:00","id":1485615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485425#post1485425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can buy the idea that most Cappadocians are happy enough with not being on the &amp;quot;to kill&amp;quot; list to let go everything else. At least they weren't in hell, and if they insist on the whole &amp;quot;sins of the father&amp;quot; thing they'll be just as guilty. Again, with the Giovanni elders that really pressed for their hunt killed in the process of formation of the Hecata, with Augustus being given a specially gruesome ritualistic end, it isn't all that unlikely that they feel avenged enough.<br /> <br /> The Lamia are weird, indeed, probably just following the Cappadocians. The Nagaraja are leaderless and clueless since Revised nuked their leadership, so they're all in for survival and whatever.<br /> <br /> But I actually have some sympathy for their original depiction, so I'm considering in my games to have the Nagaraja still in Enoch and/or now in contact with the Traditions or Disparate Alliance (they're actually an old Mage Craft and their Mages still existed until the Nuke).</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to run it is to have the Nagaraja infiltrate the Hecata as spies for the Tal'mahe'Ra, on the one hand, but also for protection now the Hand is fractured and has lost its holdings in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The Harbingers of the True Black Hand likely did the introductions. They may even have positioned them as some long-lost offshoot, rather than the death mages with stolen Setite vitae they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T08:59:30-07:00","id":1485628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483924-is-oblivion-worthless?p=1485615#post1485615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to run it is to have the Nagaraja infiltrate the Hecata as spies for the Tal'mahe'Ra, on the one hand, but also for protection now the Hand is fractured and has lost its holdings in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The Harbingers of the True Black Hand likely did the introductions. They may even have positioned them as some long-lost offshoot, rather than the death mages with stolen Setite vitae they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid, but I like their connections to proto-Euthanatoi more than the Tal'Mahe'Ra specifically.<br /> <br /> While I have nothing against the conspiracy nowadays, for me the organization itself is the least interesting thing about DSotBH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T18:09:25-07:00","id":1505520,"title":"","content":"I guess we all agree that the Lasombras, obviously, weren't in the Family Reunion. So, I don't understand why they're suddenly necromancers. For what I understand Obtenebration were a tool, just like Presence and Animalism. Unless you're a Mystic, but most Lasombras weren't. My personal feelings are that during the Sabbath debacle, was noticed that Lasombras were particularly loved, so instead of blocking them the clan was so nerfed to the point of implayability. Their weakness made them unable to do business in the current world, their signature power is a surefire way to Wassail, and they lost their sect in the most improbable way possible.<br /> But, to some people that works, and good for them, I hope they have so much fun as I had with Luciano Montanari, my almost dissociative antitribu priest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}